252
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,600
- Right on woman!

253
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:50,300
(laughing)

254
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:52,733
- She will be quite a tasty
dish to take to our king!

255
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:56,067
- I'm not that tasty,
I'm mostly gristle!

256
00:09:56,067 --> 00:09:58,667
- There's a caravan,
must be gold there!

257
00:09:58,667 --> 00:10:01,067
- [Tom] Hey, watch the
hands, don't get fresh!

258
00:10:01,067 --> 00:10:02,833
(screaming)
- Leave my child alone!

259
00:10:02,833 --> 00:10:05,033
- [Mike] Let Pat
Carroll go, you beast!

260
00:10:05,033 --> 00:10:06,533
(screaming)

261
00:10:06,533 --> 00:10:07,767
- Help!
- Dan Haggerty!

262
00:10:07,767 --> 00:10:10,133
- Hands I cannot
lift to help them.

263
00:10:10,133 --> 00:10:12,967
- [Mike] I bowled last
night and I'm pretty stiff.

264
00:10:12,967 --> 00:10:15,000
- Wagons East!

265
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,733
(dramatic music)

266
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:22,067
- [Tom] Hey, the
caterers are here!

267
00:10:22,067 --> 00:10:23,600
♪ Where are we
goin' tonight sir ♪

268
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:27,267
♪ All I know is
that I'm on my way ♪

269
00:10:27,267 --> 00:10:29,300
- [Crow] This is
not the shortcut!

270
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:31,767
(crashing)

271
00:10:31,767 --> 00:10:33,267
- [Mike] Doctor Who!

272
00:10:33,267 --> 00:10:35,733
(horses whinnying)
(hoofbeats thundering)

273
00:10:35,733 --> 00:10:39,067
- At long last, our nation says
no to renaissance festivals!

274
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:43,933
- [Tom] Finn ropin' here
at the Mongol Rodeo!

275
00:10:43,933 --> 00:10:45,533
- Spare me, I beg you!

276
00:10:45,533 --> 00:10:47,400
- [Raider] Come closer,
my blubbering one,

277
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:49,433
and let me take a look at you!

278
00:10:49,433 --> 00:10:52,233
You seem to be well-fed,
you're heavy enough!

279
00:10:52,233 --> 00:10:53,833
- [Mika] Oh, please
spare me, sire!

280
00:10:53,833 --> 00:10:56,133
I'll do anything
you wish, anything!

281
00:10:56,133 --> 00:10:58,933
- [Mike] Wash my car and pick
up Tina from piano lessons!

282
00:10:59,967 --> 00:11:02,300
- Swear you'll serve me!

283
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:04,767
- Yes sir, I will, I will!

284
00:11:04,767 --> 00:11:06,867
You can have anything I own!

285
00:11:06,867 --> 00:11:08,067
Here, see this?

286
00:11:09,567 --> 00:11:11,867
- A finger towel, great!

287
00:11:11,867 --> 00:11:15,000
- [Mike] And here's a soap
sliver, please spare my life!

288
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,200
- Listen well, son of misery!

289
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,733
- [Tom] You know my dad?

290
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:23,133
- Send this to us as a
signal to Chief Kalin

291
00:11:23,133 --> 00:11:26,400
that the Prince's soldiers
have left the city.

292
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:29,733
I shall await your signal
at the river in seven moons.

293
00:11:29,733 --> 00:11:32,633
Hear me, oh miserable one!
- Danny Kaye!

294
00:11:32,633 --> 00:11:34,967
- If you fail us,
if you deceive us,

295
00:11:34,967 --> 00:11:36,500
you shall die like a dog!

296
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:40,067
- Ah!
(Crow barking)

297
00:11:40,067 --> 00:11:41,633
(tense music)

298
00:11:41,633 --> 00:11:43,900
- [Narrator] This was a
time of giants and dragons,

299
00:11:43,900 --> 00:11:45,200
- [Mike] And low inflation.

300
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:46,833
- [Narrator] When brave
and fearless men rose up

301
00:11:46,833 --> 00:11:49,800
to perform mighty deeds
against the forces of evil.

302
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:51,067
- [Tom] I'm Mike Wallace.

303
00:11:51,067 --> 00:11:53,500
- [Narrator] Mightiest
of all was Invincor,

304
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:55,333
mighty defender
of the righteous.

305
00:11:55,333 --> 00:11:57,533
- And a nice guy!
- Who raised his magic sword

306
00:11:57,533 --> 00:11:59,533
across the breadth of the land

307
00:11:59,533 --> 00:12:01,733
to smite the
enemies of the just.

308
00:12:01,733 --> 00:12:03,033
- [Mike] Riding Lori Barbero.

309
00:12:03,033 --> 00:12:04,567
- [Narrator] After many years,

310
00:12:04,567 --> 00:12:08,900
when Invincor had grown weary
with age, his tasks were done.

311
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:11,167
- [Tom] He was given a farewell
banquet and a small TV.

312
00:12:11,167 --> 00:12:13,467
- As ye travel far and wide,

313
00:12:13,467 --> 00:12:15,067
O ye wandering pilgrims--

314
00:12:15,067 --> 00:12:16,533
- [Mike] Uh, boss?

315
00:12:16,533 --> 00:12:17,833
- Seek out a young man.

316
00:12:17,833 --> 00:12:19,333
- [Mike] Hey, boss?

317
00:12:19,333 --> 00:12:22,933
- Stout of heart, strong of
arm, and brave of spirit.

318
00:12:22,933 --> 00:12:24,267
- And taut of buttocks.

319
00:12:24,267 --> 00:12:25,867
- And when you find such a man,

320
00:12:25,867 --> 00:12:29,100
give him this, my magic sword,

321
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:31,533
to defend our land
and our people

322
00:12:31,533 --> 00:12:33,133
from all manner of enemies.

323
00:12:33,133 --> 00:12:35,233
- [Tom] And get the
five bucks he owes me.

324
00:12:36,633 --> 00:12:40,700
- [Narrator] His last deed
done, Invincor turned to stone

325
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:44,233
to become part of a legend
that would live for all time.

326
00:12:44,233 --> 00:12:46,700
- [Mike] How many prologues
does this movie need?

327
00:12:48,167 --> 00:12:50,867
- Then they harvested
the charcoal briquettes.

328
00:12:52,267 --> 00:12:54,200
- [Tom] Boy, farmers
really need the rain, huh?

329
00:12:56,100 --> 00:12:58,000
- [Mike] The heat is
blowing up my skirt!

330
00:12:58,933 --> 00:12:59,867
- [Tom] Ow.

331
00:12:59,867 --> 00:13:00,667
Ow.

332
00:13:00,667 --> 00:13:01,500
Ow.

333
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:02,333
Ow.

334
00:13:02,333 --> 00:13:03,267
Ow.

335
00:13:03,267 --> 00:13:05,300
- At least I saved this stick!

336
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:09,833
- I'm thirsty!

337
00:13:09,833 --> 00:13:10,633
- [Tom] Oh, what's your poison?

338
00:13:10,633 --> 00:13:12,133
- Patience, my son.

339
00:13:14,133 --> 00:13:15,900
- [Mike] I'm
thirsty, I'm thirsty!

340
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:17,667
Next I suppose you'll
want something to eat!

341
00:13:17,667 --> 00:13:20,500
I've never had anything to
drink and I've done just fine!

342
00:13:21,833 --> 00:13:23,333
(somber music)

343
00:13:23,333 --> 00:13:25,833
- [Tom] Ah, good, they
reached the ranger station!

344
00:13:28,333 --> 00:13:29,967
- Good morrow to thee, stranger!

345
00:13:29,967 --> 00:13:32,600
We are weary travelers,
what is thy name?

346
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:34,833
- [Ilya] I am Ilya
Muromets, son of Theodore.

347
00:13:34,833 --> 00:13:36,267
- [Mike] You pay at
the first window.

348
00:13:36,267 --> 00:13:37,667
- Could you bring us some water?

349
00:13:37,667 --> 00:13:39,000
- [Ilya] Glad would
I be to serve you

350
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,900
but I cannot move
from this chair.

351
00:13:40,900 --> 00:13:43,300
Come into my house
and drink your fill.

352
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:44,367
- Thank you!

353
00:13:44,367 --> 00:13:45,600
Come!

354
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:47,833
- I should warn you,
I'm just a torso!

355
00:13:47,833 --> 00:13:49,600
- [Tom] They're at
Jellystone Park.

356
00:13:51,067 --> 00:13:53,067
- [Mike] He's got
a poster of Sun Ra!

357
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:56,567
- Greetings to thee, Ilya.

358
00:13:56,567 --> 00:13:58,700
- Yeah yeah, could you
bring me a magazine?

359
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:01,333
- I know you gentle pilgrims
have traveled far and wide.

360
00:14:01,333 --> 00:14:02,533
- [Tom] Member of FDIC.

361
00:14:02,533 --> 00:14:03,933
- Tell me of the evils
that have befallen

362
00:14:03,933 --> 00:14:06,867
our beloved country in
these days of darkness.

363
00:14:06,867 --> 00:14:08,433
- Our poor and troubled land

364
00:14:08,433 --> 00:14:11,100
is plunged into woe
deep as the sea!

365
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:14,667
Those cursed Tugars
plunder, rob, and kill!

366
00:14:14,667 --> 00:14:16,567
- If only I had
my strength back,

367
00:14:17,933 --> 00:14:20,200
I could help defend my
country in her hour of need.

368
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:22,333
- But I've been classified 4-F.

369
00:14:24,133 --> 00:14:25,767
- [Tom] I could
beat this guy up!

370
00:14:27,067 --> 00:14:28,933
- Drink the dew of
the magic grass, sir,

371
00:14:28,933 --> 00:14:30,933
and perhaps thy
strength will return.

372
00:14:30,933 --> 00:14:32,300
- [Mike] Here's
some Haley's M.O.

373
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:33,300
- Thank you, my son.

374
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:39,367
Drink this, young man,
drink hearty and pray.

375
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:43,100
- [Tom] Please sir,
could I have more?

376
00:14:45,167 --> 00:14:47,100
- [Mike] Ilya likes
carrots, doesn't he?

377
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:48,467
- Doest thou feel the strength

378
00:14:48,467 --> 00:14:50,400
returning to thy
veins yet, Ilya?

379
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:51,600
- I'm less thirsty.

380
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:52,900
- Yes yes, I can!

381
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:54,867
- [Tom] I'm coppin' a buzz!

382
00:14:54,867 --> 00:14:56,233
- But...

383
00:14:56,233 --> 00:14:58,100
- [Tom] The walls are moving!

384
00:14:58,100 --> 00:14:59,967
(Ilya groaning)
- Splat!

385
00:14:59,967 --> 00:15:01,933
- I still cannot move!

386
00:15:01,933 --> 00:15:03,100
- Patience, my Ilya.

387
00:15:04,533 --> 00:15:07,100
Thy strength shall indeed
return, I promise thee.

388
00:15:08,300 --> 00:15:10,467
- [Mike] Uh, hold on,
I'm havin' a montage.

389
00:15:10,467 --> 00:15:12,700
(tense music)

390
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:14,400
- It's the line
for Wild Mountain!

391
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,967
- [Tom] Whoa, that was
one a high colonic,

392
00:15:21,967 --> 00:15:23,900
yes sir, I feel like a new man!

393
00:15:30,033 --> 00:15:32,433
- Let's get you back to
your room, Mr. Togolson.

394
00:15:33,767 --> 00:15:35,000
- [Mike] I'll take these,

395
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,133
I'll just wear them
out of the store!

396
00:15:37,133 --> 00:15:38,800
- [Tom] I feel good all under!

397
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:41,633
First thing, I take
off the burlap dress!

398
00:15:41,633 --> 00:15:44,533
(triumphant music)

399
00:15:46,333 --> 00:15:47,733
- [Mike] And now,
ladies and gentlemen,

400
00:15:47,733 --> 00:15:49,767
the Swedish Moses of Soul!

401
00:15:50,933 --> 00:15:52,700
- [Tom] Ah, hey, who
left all my tools

402
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:54,800
laying around in the front yard?

403
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:57,100
- [Mike] I'm feeling
positively demonstrative!

404
00:15:57,100 --> 00:15:59,400
I could almost tell
my wife I love her!

405
00:16:01,967 --> 00:16:04,767
- Oh, I need to sit down for
a while, believe it or not.

406
00:16:06,233 --> 00:16:08,167
- Take now the magic sword of
Invincor and be thou like him.

407
00:16:08,167 --> 00:16:10,600
- [Tom] 'Cause we don't
want to carry it anymore!

408
00:16:15,700 --> 00:16:17,833
- [Mike] This is the
best tasting sword ever!

409
00:16:17,833 --> 00:16:19,367
- Thank you, good friends.

410
00:16:19,367 --> 00:16:21,967
(upbeat music)

411
00:16:25,733 --> 00:16:28,667
- [Tom] Ah, I sold the sword
and bought some Finnish vodka.

412
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,500
- [Mike] Yep, pretty much!

413
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:34,167
- (sighing) How my hands yearn
to feel the good, rich earth

414
00:16:34,167 --> 00:16:36,500
and the honest toil of
the farmer once again.

415
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:38,533
- Well, go ahead and
grab a plow, then!

416
00:16:38,533 --> 00:16:40,500
- Work the fields
with my father.

417
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:43,100
- [Tom] I thought
he was the father?

418
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:45,033
- [Mike] It's a
good crop of stumps!

419
00:16:46,267 --> 00:16:47,500
(cracking)

420
00:16:47,500 --> 00:16:49,600
- Uh, hold on, I'll
get the Bobcat!

421
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:50,500
- [Tom] Ow!

422
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:52,033
(Ilya grunting)
(cracking)

423
00:16:52,033 --> 00:16:53,233
- [Tom] Uh, we want that.

424
00:16:53,233 --> 00:16:54,967
- Root up the tree stumps!

425
00:16:54,967 --> 00:16:57,233
- [Mike] And we'll have
a tree stump of fun!

426
00:16:57,233 --> 00:16:59,500
(crashing)

427
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,233
(Ilya grunting)

428
00:17:02,233 --> 00:17:04,433
- I'll see how many
times I can skip this!

429
00:17:05,433 --> 00:17:06,633
(splashing)

430
00:17:06,633 --> 00:17:07,567
- [Tom] Sure, go ahead
and use the fjord

431
00:17:07,567 --> 00:17:09,100
for your garbage dump, Ilya!

432
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:12,167
- Hard as stone now has been
no earth of my father's.

433
00:17:12,167 --> 00:17:13,400
- [Mike] Grandpa, no!

434
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:16,633
- Soft as the down of a
swan will thou become.

435
00:17:16,633 --> 00:17:18,467
- The mighty falcon
lifts his wings

436
00:17:18,467 --> 00:17:20,300
and is ready to fly again.

437
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:21,867
- Our son is like a man reborn!

438
00:17:21,867 --> 00:17:24,400
- His strong hands shall
help work our fields.

439
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:26,167
- The banjo becomes
angry at midnight!

440
00:17:26,167 --> 00:17:27,500
What the hell are
you talking about?

441
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:29,133
- Forgive me, dear mother.

442
00:17:29,133 --> 00:17:30,400
- [Tom] I overreacted.

443
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:33,667
- But I cannot till the
land or reap its riches.

444
00:17:33,667 --> 00:17:36,300
Kalin and his plunderers
aim their deadly arrows

445
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:38,667
at the heart of our country
at this very moment.

446
00:17:38,667 --> 00:17:40,133
- [Mike] Oh well!

447
00:17:40,133 --> 00:17:43,000
- I cannot remain here
while our country suffers.

448
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,100
- So you're coppin' our again?

449
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:46,200
- Give me your
blessing, dear parents.

450
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:47,300
- [Tom] You want
the car, don't ya?

451
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:49,100
- Now I must go forth.

452
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:51,667
- What you tell us lies
heavy on my heart, my son.

453
00:17:51,667 --> 00:17:55,233
- I go because I must,
Mother, my country needs me!

454
00:17:55,233 --> 00:17:58,500
- I give you my blessing,
Ilya my son, go in peace.

455
00:17:58,500 --> 00:18:00,933
- [Mike] Why are you
older than me, son?

456
00:18:00,933 --> 00:18:04,533
- Guard against evil, my son,
and help your fellow man.

457
00:18:04,533 --> 00:18:05,900
- [Tom] But not Murray.

458
00:18:05,900 --> 00:18:08,333
- I shall remember your
wishes always, Mother.

459
00:18:09,767 --> 00:18:12,300
- Hey, hey hey hey, hey hey,
you're in the wrong myth!

460
00:18:13,367 --> 00:18:15,600
- You will need a strong horse,

461
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:17,867
I would like to
give you mine, Ilya.

462
00:18:17,867 --> 00:18:19,700
His name is Chestnut Gray.

463
00:18:19,700 --> 00:18:21,167
- [Mike] Oh, that's
okay, I'll walk.

464
00:18:21,167 --> 00:18:22,767
(Chestnut Gray whinnying)

465
00:18:22,767 --> 00:18:25,700
- Do not concern yourself
over his small size.

466
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:27,900
Bathe him three times in due

467
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:29,800
and he will grow
until he becomes

468
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:32,767
the mightiest of all the
steeds you have ever known.

469
00:18:32,767 --> 00:18:34,767
- [Tom] Jeez, I'm
running late as it is!

470
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:37,833
- Well, let's get
you far enough away

471
00:18:37,833 --> 00:18:39,500
where they won't
hear the gunshot.

472
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:40,967
- [Tom] No!

473
00:18:40,967 --> 00:18:42,800
- [Ilya] Grow,
Chestnut Gray, grow!

474
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:46,567
- Isn't he supposed to bathe
him in Mountain Dew or?

475
00:18:46,567 --> 00:18:50,067
- [Ilya] He thou as fleet
of foot as the deer.

476
00:18:50,067 --> 00:18:52,100
- [Tom] Buy bonds
where you work or bank.

477
00:18:53,933 --> 00:18:57,200
- [Ilya] Swim rivers
faster than the salmon.

478
00:18:57,200 --> 00:19:00,867
Streak across the ground
swifter than the wolf.

479
00:19:00,867 --> 00:19:03,767
Higher than the Falcon
winging through the sky.

480
00:19:03,767 --> 00:19:07,167
- [Mike] Longer than there've
been fishes in the ocean.

481
00:19:07,167 --> 00:19:10,700
- [Ilya] When a stranger
calls, hear him not,

482
00:19:10,700 --> 00:19:13,300
but when you hear my voice--
- Run!

483
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:15,900
- [Ilya] Come swiftly
like the wind.

484
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:17,467
- Anything else, Your Highness?

485
00:19:17,467 --> 00:19:19,900
- [Ilya] And we shall
be friends unto death,

486
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:21,633
in deed and in battle.

487
00:19:21,633 --> 00:19:23,500
- [Mike] Oh, I don't do battle!

488
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:25,033
- [Ilya] Good Chestnut Gray.

489
00:19:25,033 --> 00:19:28,000
- [Tom] Look, I got an
offer from Calumet Farms.

490
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,600
- [Ilya] Serve me
well, noble steed.

491
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:32,700
- [Mike] He is a
lonely, lonely man.

492
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:35,700
- Connery!

493
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:36,700
Snipes!

494
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:41,000
- [Tom] Daily affirmations.

495
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,933
- [Mike] The Duluth Chamber
of Commerce bids you adieu.

496
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:50,033
- And wherever Ilya went
he carried his pool cue.

497
00:19:50,033 --> 00:19:52,767
- [Tom] Aw jeez, he cast
it right into the weeds!

498
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:56,233
(majestic music)

499
00:19:56,233 --> 00:19:57,433
(raven cawing)

500
00:19:57,433 --> 00:19:58,633
- [Mike] Nevermore!

501
00:19:58,633 --> 00:20:00,400
- [Cryptic Voice]
Follow the right road

502
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:02,433
and you will find riches!

503
00:20:02,433 --> 00:20:04,200
- [Deep Voice]
Follow the left road

504
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:06,800
and you will find a wife!

505
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:11,800
- [Eerie Voice] Go straight
ahead and you will find dead!

506
00:20:12,967 --> 00:20:14,533
- Chestnut Gray, quit
doin' your impressions!

507
00:20:14,533 --> 00:20:16,500
- [Ilya] Riches would
give me little joy.

508
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:17,733
- [Tom] But I'll
take 'em anyway.

509
00:20:17,733 --> 00:20:19,667
- Now is no time
to woo me a wife!

510
00:20:19,667 --> 00:20:21,133
- [Tom] But I'll
take one anyway.

511
00:20:21,133 --> 00:20:24,133
- [Ilya] So I shall follow
the road that leads to death!

512
00:20:24,133 --> 00:20:26,167
- I might not get
to death tonight,

513
00:20:26,167 --> 00:20:28,300
I may spend the night
at serious injury

514
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:30,967
and head over to primitive
disability in the morning.

515
00:20:32,267 --> 00:20:35,600
♪ No I don't wanna fall ♪

516
00:20:38,533 --> 00:20:40,500
Chen, round up every
Finn on the island!

517
00:20:46,067 --> 00:20:47,467
- Thou shalt seek shelter

518
00:20:47,467 --> 00:20:49,467
in the southwest
corner of thy basement!

519
00:20:50,533 --> 00:20:52,500
(bird screeching)

520
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:54,267
- [Mike] Where are the RUOSes?

521
00:20:56,567 --> 00:20:58,833
- Oh, this is downtown death.

522
00:20:58,833 --> 00:21:00,867
(bird screeching)

523
00:21:00,867 --> 00:21:02,167
- [Tom] Woo woo!

524
00:21:05,367 --> 00:21:09,033
- This movie has a real
View-Master quality.

525
00:21:10,167 --> 00:21:12,300
- [Mike] Oh, why did
Invincor like this job?

526
00:21:13,367 --> 00:21:15,733
(Chestnut Gray whinnying)

527
00:21:15,733 --> 00:21:17,600
(Ilya grunting)

528
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:20,400
- [Wind Demon] Go straight
ahead and you will find death!

529
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:21,333
- Ah!
- Ugh!

530
00:21:21,333 --> 00:21:23,233
Maybe he has a good personality?

531
00:21:23,233 --> 00:21:24,700
(dramatic music)

532
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:26,967
- Whoa, blech, Dorito breath!

533
00:21:31,367 --> 00:21:33,667
- [Tom] Dizzy Gillespie-esque.

534
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:35,100
- [Mike] Well,
that's always nice,

535
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:37,067
just blow the leaves
into the neighbor's yard!

536
00:21:38,167 --> 00:21:40,267
- Couldn't the
wind just cry Mary?

537
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:46,967
- Do not fear this wind demon!

538
00:21:46,967 --> 00:21:48,533
- [Mike] You know,
sometimes I wake up

539
00:21:48,533 --> 00:21:50,333
and I feel like this guy looks.

540
00:21:52,733 --> 00:21:56,533
- [Ilya] He cannot harm
you, Chestnut Gray!

541
00:21:56,533 --> 00:21:58,833
- [Tom] Yeah, sure, let's go
down the road to death, fine,

542
00:21:58,833 --> 00:22:01,233
what the hell was I thinkin'?

543
00:22:02,667 --> 00:22:05,567
- Chestnut Gray is like the
Chevy Suburban of horses.

544
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:07,733
(crashing)

545
00:22:07,733 --> 00:22:08,633
(laughing)
- Yeah, sure.

546
00:22:08,633 --> 00:22:09,800
- Yeah.
- Lucky shot!

547
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:15,400
- [Tom] Uh, I can
explain everything, heh!

548
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:17,633
- Looks like a fat owl this one

549
00:22:17,633 --> 00:22:19,767
and yet he cries
rivers of tears!

550
00:22:19,767 --> 00:22:21,333
- I'm a wind demon, it's my job!

551
00:22:21,333 --> 00:22:22,700
- I shall take you to my Prince

552
00:22:22,700 --> 00:22:24,733
and he will decide
what to do with you.

553
00:22:24,733 --> 00:22:26,667
- [Mike] Okay, let me
put on my good fur.

554
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,533
- Princes, nobles, and warriors,

555
00:22:29,533 --> 00:22:31,300
here I sit with you in judgment

556
00:22:31,300 --> 00:22:33,233
and here with you
do I hold court.

557
00:22:33,233 --> 00:22:34,867
If there be any wrongdoers,

558
00:22:34,867 --> 00:22:37,067
let them be brought
before us for judgment.

559
00:22:37,067 --> 00:22:38,833
- Bring up Al D'Amato!

560
00:22:38,833 --> 00:22:42,133
(crowd murmuring)

561
00:22:42,133 --> 00:22:43,967
- [Tom] I like
having court outside!

562
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:47,900
- This villain must be
punished, good Prince,

563
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:49,867
he tore my mare's tail off!

564
00:22:49,867 --> 00:22:51,333
You must find a
suitable punishment,

565
00:22:51,333 --> 00:22:53,433
for what he has
done is a bad thing!

566
00:22:53,433 --> 00:22:55,033
- It is bad.

567
00:22:55,033 --> 00:22:56,900
- He has also stolen
the Royal timber!

568
00:22:56,900 --> 00:22:58,567
- He must be a villain!

569
00:22:58,567 --> 00:22:59,933
- Yes, sire!
- Kris Kristofferson!

570
00:22:59,933 --> 00:23:02,533
- It is true that
I did these things,

571
00:23:02,533 --> 00:23:04,333
but I had very
good reason, sire!

572
00:23:04,333 --> 00:23:06,333
He loaned me his
horse but no harness,

573
00:23:06,333 --> 00:23:08,433
so I tied the wagon
to the horse's tail.

574
00:23:08,433 --> 00:23:09,367
(crowd laughing)

575
00:23:09,367 --> 00:23:10,867
That is how it happened, sire.

576
00:23:10,867 --> 00:23:12,733
- Ha ha, it's the Finnish
version of Night Court!

577
00:23:12,733 --> 00:23:15,300
- He should be sent to
prison, he must be punished!

578
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:17,400
- This is our verdict.

579
00:23:17,400 --> 00:23:18,867
- I'll allow the DNA.

580
00:23:18,867 --> 00:23:22,300
- You, Vagaran, give
him your horse to ride

581
00:23:22,300 --> 00:23:25,900
through the forest until her
tail shall grow back again.

582
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:27,133
This is our judgment.

583
00:23:27,133 --> 00:23:28,400
- Justice, Region
Prince, justice!

584
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:30,000
- [Tom] Get up, you brown noser!

585
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,333
- And you, young man, remember
you must return the horse

586
00:23:32,333 --> 00:23:34,200
to Vagaran in good condition.

587
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:35,100
- And enter drug rehab!

588
00:23:35,100 --> 00:23:36,333
- Yes, sire.

589
00:23:36,333 --> 00:23:37,567
I swear it!

590
00:23:37,567 --> 00:23:39,100
- [Mike] It's a kingdom
of Robert Borks!

591
00:23:39,100 --> 00:23:40,600
- Radiant Prince!

592
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:43,467
Durbar the mighty warrior
has returned to the palace.

593
00:23:43,467 --> 00:23:45,567
- [Tom] He's the artist formerly
known as Radiant Prince.

594
00:23:45,567 --> 00:23:47,600
- Summon all the nobles
for a great feast

595
00:23:48,767 --> 00:23:51,300
and see that all these
people are fed well!

596
00:23:51,300 --> 00:23:52,433
- I need a veggie meal!

597
00:23:52,433 --> 00:23:53,567
- [Tom] Can I bring my cousin?

598
00:23:53,567 --> 00:23:55,133
- [Mike] I'm lactose-intolerant!

599
00:23:55,133 --> 00:23:56,833
- [Crow] Can I have
the money instead?

600
00:23:56,833 --> 00:23:58,100
- [Tom] But I don't like food!

601
00:23:58,100 --> 00:23:59,567
- Our good and noble
Prince invites you all

602
00:23:59,567 --> 00:24:01,067
to the feast at the palace!

603
00:24:01,067 --> 00:24:02,367
(clanking)

604
00:24:02,367 --> 00:24:04,933
(beeping)

605
00:24:04,933 --> 00:24:07,800
(whirring)

606
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:08,700
(thudding)

607
00:24:08,700 --> 00:24:10,600
(whooshing)

608
00:24:10,600 --> 00:24:11,533
(thudding)

609
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:12,700
(clicking)

610
00:24:12,700 --> 00:24:15,267
(loud ticking)

611
00:24:40,500 --> 00:24:45,100
- Once, on the shore on
the great Northern Sea,

612
00:24:46,667 --> 00:24:51,100
two men stood alone on a pier.

613
00:24:51,100 --> 00:24:56,100
(wind whistling)
(waves crashing)

614
00:25:02,367 --> 00:25:03,200
- Sven?

615
00:25:26,133 --> 00:25:26,967
- Ja, Ole?

616
00:25:34,033 --> 00:25:36,867
(foghorn blaring)

617
00:25:48,800 --> 00:25:53,067
- There came in to me a thought.

618
00:25:57,800 --> 00:26:00,733
(seabirds calling)

619
00:26:15,100 --> 00:26:16,067
- Ja?

620
00:26:25,267 --> 00:26:27,767
(dog barking)

621
00:26:40,967 --> 00:26:45,967
- I will count the
boards of this pier.

622
00:26:52,600 --> 00:26:53,400
- Ja?

623
00:26:58,700 --> 00:27:00,133
- And you...

624
00:27:02,700 --> 00:27:03,533
- Ja?

625
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:13,600
- You will count the
slits between the boards.

626
00:27:18,433 --> 00:27:21,233
- You the boards

627
00:27:23,333 --> 00:27:27,267
and I the slits.

628
00:27:29,767 --> 00:27:30,600
- Ja.

629
00:27:33,967 --> 00:27:36,867
(seabirds calling)

630
00:27:38,600 --> 00:27:40,333
- (gasping) Begin!

631
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:45,833
- One.

632
00:27:47,033 --> 00:27:47,867
- One.

633
00:27:49,267 --> 00:27:50,100
- Two.

634
00:27:51,567 --> 00:27:52,400
- Two.

635
00:27:53,867 --> 00:27:54,700
- Three.

636
00:27:56,300 --> 00:27:57,100
- Three.

637
00:27:59,000 --> 00:27:59,800
- Four.

638
00:28:01,500 --> 00:28:02,300
- Four.

639
00:28:03,767 --> 00:28:04,600
- Five.

640
00:28:06,300 --> 00:28:07,133
- Five.

641
00:28:08,567 --> 00:28:09,400
- Six.

642
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:11,700
- Six (yelping).

643
00:28:12,800 --> 00:28:15,133
(splashing)

644
00:28:17,800 --> 00:28:20,133
- And so you see,

645
00:28:21,900 --> 00:28:24,933
when you're out of slits,

646
00:28:26,300 --> 00:28:29,433
you're out of pier.

647
00:28:32,433 --> 00:28:34,933
(dog barking)

648
00:28:42,133 --> 00:28:46,500
(crowd singing in
foreign language)

649
00:28:46,500 --> 00:28:49,500
- [Crow] It may be the wine,
Lars, but you're a pretty man.

650
00:28:49,500 --> 00:28:51,333
- [Tom] Sven, no,
don't, you mustn't!

651
00:28:53,300 --> 00:28:54,667
- [Mike] Who's the new guy?

652
00:28:56,133 --> 00:28:58,000
- [Tom] We'll be showing
the Vikes-Packers game

653
00:28:58,000 --> 00:28:59,667
in just a few minutes everyone.

654
00:29:00,833 --> 00:29:01,900
- Excuse me, good people.

655
00:29:01,900 --> 00:29:03,133
- [Mike] Where's the men's room?

656
00:29:03,133 --> 00:29:05,800
- Which among you
is Prince Vanda?

657
00:29:05,800 --> 00:29:07,233
- Why do you ask for the Prince?

658
00:29:07,233 --> 00:29:09,133
A bumpkin like
you belongs there,

659
00:29:09,133 --> 00:29:11,400
at the foot of the
table with the peasants.

660
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:13,300
- You are too harsh with
the stranger, Alexi,

661
00:29:13,300 --> 00:29:15,900
let him be heard, perhaps
he brings important news.

662
00:29:15,900 --> 00:29:17,900
- Yeah, like we're
the best buffets are.

663
00:29:19,100 --> 00:29:21,000
- I came here not to
feast, good nobles,

664
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:23,767
but to serve my
Prince and my country.

665
00:29:23,767 --> 00:29:25,200
- And I say you're
not fit to sit

666
00:29:25,200 --> 00:29:26,633
at the same table with a noble!

667
00:29:26,633 --> 00:29:27,700
- [Mike] No no no no no no!

668
00:29:27,700 --> 00:29:29,500
- You, a noble?

669
00:29:29,500 --> 00:29:32,300
More likely you joust with
milkmaids behind the barn!

670
00:29:32,300 --> 00:29:33,133
- [Tom] I'm not gay!

671
00:29:33,133 --> 00:29:35,633
(crowd laughing)

672
00:29:35,633 --> 00:29:38,500
- He's the Finnish Oscar Wilde!

673
00:29:38,500 --> 00:29:40,333
- Make way for the Nobel Mika,

674
00:29:40,333 --> 00:29:42,767
bearing rare and costly
gifts for our Prince!

675
00:29:42,767 --> 00:29:46,067
- Good health and
greetings, Radiant Prince.

676
00:29:46,067 --> 00:29:47,500
- [Mike] Look, I don't
book openers anymore.

677
00:29:47,500 --> 00:29:49,867
- I have collected all
taxes and tributes.

678
00:29:49,867 --> 00:29:53,600
I was sorely wounded in
battle but I routed them all!

679
00:29:53,600 --> 00:29:55,167
All your enemies!

680
00:29:55,167 --> 00:29:56,667
- [Tom] Anyways, here's
some of the stuff we got.

681
00:29:56,667 --> 00:29:59,667
- For you, dear Prince, for
you alone I would do it again,

682
00:29:59,667 --> 00:30:01,367
I would gladly lay down my life.

683
00:30:01,367 --> 00:30:02,800
- For a hamburger today!

684
00:30:02,800 --> 00:30:05,200
- Radient Prince, I
bested the mighty Tsartag,

685
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:07,100
for you I would
gladly give my life!

686
00:30:07,100 --> 00:30:08,333
- [Mike] No, no lick!

687
00:30:08,333 --> 00:30:10,567
- So would we all,
every one of us!

688
00:30:10,567 --> 00:30:12,300
- A wind demon attacked me

689
00:30:12,300 --> 00:30:14,733
and I cut him to ribbons
in the enchanted forest!

690
00:30:14,733 --> 00:30:16,200
- He lies, my Prince!

691
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:18,100
- [Tom] I saw him wet them
on the field of honor!

692
00:30:18,100 --> 00:30:21,133
- I know that he has not even
set eyes on the wind demon.

693
00:30:21,133 --> 00:30:24,867
- Who are you, good stranger,
and where do you come from?

694
00:30:24,867 --> 00:30:28,367
- I am Ilya Muromets,
I am from Goldova,

695
00:30:28,367 --> 00:30:31,000
my father has a small
farm there near the river.

696
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:32,400
- Oops, dropped a cufflink.

697
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:34,900
- And have you yourself
seen the wind demon?

698
00:30:34,900 --> 00:30:37,200
- [Ilya] I will show him to you!

699
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:38,467
- [Mike] Say hello to the
nice people, wind demon!

700
00:30:38,467 --> 00:30:40,933
- Here he is, the
evil one, not very big

701
00:30:40,933 --> 00:30:42,267
but he's as mean as he looks!

702
00:30:42,267 --> 00:30:43,733
- [Man] I've never
seen such a monster!

703
00:30:43,733 --> 00:30:45,200
Command him to whistle
as loud as he can!

704
00:30:45,200 --> 00:30:47,800
- [Woman] Can he
really create the wind?

705
00:30:47,800 --> 00:30:50,733
- [Ilya] That he can do but
do not let him frighten you!

706
00:30:50,733 --> 00:30:51,933
- [Tom] Do you eat lunch?

707
00:30:51,933 --> 00:30:54,567
- Wait Alicia, please
do not run away.

708
00:30:54,567 --> 00:30:55,800
- [Mike] Wang Chung with me!

709
00:30:55,800 --> 00:30:57,833
- Someone will see us here!

710
00:30:57,833 --> 00:31:00,500
- I do not care as
long as we're together!

711
00:31:00,500 --> 00:31:03,733
- My brothers say I'm too
young to be wooed, Alexi.

712
00:31:03,733 --> 00:31:05,467
- Statutory woo!

713
00:31:05,467 --> 00:31:06,833
- You belong to me, Alicia.

714
00:31:08,467 --> 00:31:10,367
(gasping)
- Oh, Captain Spaulding!

715
00:31:10,367 --> 00:31:12,667
- Now whistle, you
ugly wind demon,

716
00:31:12,667 --> 00:31:14,500
but only with half
of your strength!

717
00:31:15,333 --> 00:31:16,833
- Clint Howard!

718
00:31:16,833 --> 00:31:19,333
(Tom huffing)

719
00:31:20,700 --> 00:31:23,033
- Now whistle, evil one, mm!

720
00:31:23,033 --> 00:31:24,467
- [Mike] You know how
to whistle, don't you?

721
00:31:24,467 --> 00:31:25,833
(wind demon heaving)

722
00:31:25,833 --> 00:31:27,233
(wind demon whistling)

723
00:31:27,233 --> 00:31:29,267
- Oh yuck, he was
eating crackers!

724
00:31:29,267 --> 00:31:31,467
(dramatic music)

725
00:31:31,467 --> 00:31:36,467
♪ The summer wind
demon came blowin' in ♪

726
00:31:37,233 --> 00:31:39,700
♪ Roll up the barrels ♪

727
00:31:39,700 --> 00:31:41,967
- Cleanups a breeze
thanks to wind demon!

728
00:31:46,567 --> 00:31:48,133
- Alicia!
- Wacky sight gags

729
00:31:48,133 --> 00:31:50,067
of ancient Finlandia.

730
00:31:50,067 --> 00:31:51,433
- [Tom] Mrs. Rittenhouse!

731
00:31:53,467 --> 00:31:54,800
- Man, I'm killin' tonight!

732
00:31:56,800 --> 00:31:59,400
- [Mike] The wind
hooked me to a cable!

733
00:31:59,400 --> 00:32:03,033
♪ Everyone knows it's Windy ♪

734
00:32:05,033 --> 00:32:07,133
- [Mike] The wind demon
has killed a lot of people

735
00:32:07,133 --> 00:32:08,967
but it's all in good fun!

736
00:32:08,967 --> 00:32:11,533
- Stop him Ilya, make him stop!

737
00:32:11,533 --> 00:32:13,833
- Stop him before
he blows us away!

738
00:32:13,833 --> 00:32:16,533
- Stop, we've seen
enough, make him stop!

739
00:32:16,533 --> 00:32:18,000
- Hold your breath,
spawn of the devil,

740
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:20,067
you have performed
your last evil deed!

741
00:32:20,067 --> 00:32:21,267
- Hey, you asked me!

742
00:32:21,267 --> 00:32:23,300
- No more children with
your blasts of wind!

743
00:32:23,300 --> 00:32:25,533
- This country bumpkin is
quite a fellow, I think!

744
00:32:25,533 --> 00:32:27,100
- [Mike] Yes, jolly
good, old man.

745
00:32:27,100 --> 00:32:28,867
- [Tom] Ergidda,
ergidda, ergidda!

746
00:32:31,567 --> 00:32:33,400
- Oh yuck, he's in the spittoon!

747
00:32:33,400 --> 00:32:35,567
- [Mike] That was pretty
good, can he scat?

748
00:32:36,933 --> 00:32:39,800
- Take this, Ilya, as a
reward for your service.

749
00:32:41,167 --> 00:32:44,100
As for this demon, his
reward will match his deeds.

750
00:32:44,100 --> 00:32:46,300
- [Tom] Put him in
my private chambers.

751
00:32:46,300 --> 00:32:49,233
(wind demon hissing)

752
00:32:49,233 --> 00:32:50,967
- I gotta blow, ha ha ha!

753
00:32:52,433 --> 00:32:54,333
- [Alexi] You are a man
after my own heart, Ilya.

754
00:32:54,333 --> 00:32:55,700
- [Mike] Wanna start a band?

755
00:32:57,200 --> 00:32:59,667
- [Tom] And so ZZ Top was born!

756
00:32:59,667 --> 00:33:01,833
- Take no offense of Alexi,
he has a quick temper

757
00:33:01,833 --> 00:33:03,867
but he is a brave and
courageous soldier.

758
00:33:03,867 --> 00:33:04,900
Let us be friends.

759
00:33:04,900 --> 00:33:06,133
- I'm Bob from Marketing.

760
00:33:07,467 --> 00:33:09,267
(triumphant music)

761
00:33:09,267 --> 00:33:10,233
- We shall be friends!

762
00:33:10,233 --> 00:33:11,167
(buzzing)

763
00:33:11,167 --> 00:33:12,400
- Friends to the end, Ilya!

764
00:33:12,400 --> 00:33:13,967
Your steed beside my own!

765
00:33:13,967 --> 00:33:15,800
- Now let us make a pledge.

766
00:33:15,800 --> 00:33:17,800
We shall be as brothers,
the three of us.

767
00:33:17,800 --> 00:33:19,300
The younger brother
must heed the elder

768
00:33:19,300 --> 00:33:20,967
and together we
shall venture forth.

769
00:33:20,967 --> 00:33:23,500
- Together in good
and in bad we three!

770
00:33:23,500 --> 00:33:25,200
- All for one and one for all!

771
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:27,200
- Yow!
- This must be our way.

772
00:33:27,200 --> 00:33:30,100
Our country we shall defend
with our lives if we must!

773
00:33:30,100 --> 00:33:32,000
- Bravo, Ilya Muromets!

774
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:34,400
- [Crowd] Bravo, Ilya Muromets!

775
00:33:34,400 --> 00:33:35,633
Bravo, Ilya Muromets!

776
00:33:35,633 --> 00:33:36,567
- [Prince] Put on the
armor for the noble,

777
00:33:36,567 --> 00:33:37,633
Ilya, you have earned it!

778
00:33:38,500 --> 00:33:40,233
- I thank you, Prince!

779
00:33:40,233 --> 00:33:41,667
- Bad tidings, O Prince,

780
00:33:41,667 --> 00:33:43,800
Kalin's envoys have
arrived at the city gates!

781
00:33:45,067 --> 00:33:47,800
♪ We got a great big envoy ♪

782
00:33:47,800 --> 00:33:48,967
- [Tom] Pavarotti
tour is in town!

783
00:33:48,967 --> 00:33:50,867
(dramatic music)

784
00:33:50,867 --> 00:33:52,167
- [Mike] Close the buffet!

785
00:33:55,600 --> 00:33:56,733
- He's gonna blow!

786
00:33:58,200 --> 00:34:00,400
- [Prince] Greet them
with bread and salt!

787
00:34:00,400 --> 00:34:02,100
- Those swine who
laid waste our land,

788
00:34:02,100 --> 00:34:04,300
I would rather
greet them with arms

789
00:34:04,300 --> 00:34:06,000
than with bread and salt, sire!

790
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:08,467
- Those are very
bold words, Ilya.

791
00:34:08,467 --> 00:34:10,500
Would you teach me how to rule?

792
00:34:10,500 --> 00:34:12,567
First we shall hear this envoy,

793
00:34:12,567 --> 00:34:14,667
then we shall decide
what course to take.

794
00:34:14,667 --> 00:34:17,167
- [Mike] All right, if
that's how you wanna do it.

795
00:34:19,633 --> 00:34:21,800
- [Tom] Sounds like
the stripper's on next.

796
00:34:23,133 --> 00:34:25,433
- Somebody get me a
bucket, I'm gonna throw up!

797
00:34:25,433 --> 00:34:28,967
- I come as an envoy from
the mighty Chief Kalin.

798
00:34:28,967 --> 00:34:32,800
It is his will that you shall
pay him taxes and tributes.

799
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:35,633
For 12 years you must
pay these tributes to us,

800
00:34:35,633 --> 00:34:38,167
else we will invade your
land and empty your coffers!

801
00:34:38,167 --> 00:34:39,300
- [Mike] Damn liberals!

802
00:34:40,467 --> 00:34:42,100
- [Prince] Eat and
drink your fill.

803
00:34:42,100 --> 00:34:44,100
We shall pay what you ask,
we shall do what you command.

804
00:34:44,100 --> 00:34:46,000
- [Tom] Here's your
appetizer, sir.

805
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:47,467
(clattering)

806
00:34:47,467 --> 00:34:48,733
- Kalin's envoy (snorting)

807
00:34:48,733 --> 00:34:51,067
shall not be bribed
with bread and salt!

808
00:34:51,067 --> 00:34:53,500
- To send such a dolt as
an envoy is an insult!

809
00:34:53,500 --> 00:34:56,233
- Does he not look like
a great fat ox to you?

810
00:34:56,233 --> 00:34:58,367
- Who dares speak
such to Kalin's envoy?

811
00:34:58,367 --> 00:35:00,800
I would strike him down
as soon as look at him!

812
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:02,733
Guard your tongue
or I'll cut it off!

813
00:35:02,733 --> 00:35:04,667
- You come here
with words of war,

814
00:35:04,667 --> 00:35:08,067
therefore we answer in
kind and we are prepared.

815
00:35:08,067 --> 00:35:09,900
- Resistance is useless!

816
00:35:09,900 --> 00:35:12,367
I will make you bow to
our mighty Chief Kalin!

817
00:35:12,367 --> 00:35:13,600
- Your words of your boasting

818
00:35:13,600 --> 00:35:16,400
shall die in your
throat, envoy of Kalin!

819
00:35:16,400 --> 00:35:17,633
- I have heard enough!

820
00:35:17,633 --> 00:35:19,867
Your head shall be
the first I chop off!

821
00:35:19,867 --> 00:35:21,467
(whooshing)

822
00:35:21,467 --> 00:35:23,433
- [Tom] Oh, it's a
Matt Groening gargoyle!

823
00:35:25,433 --> 00:35:29,733
- By your own sword,
dog, you shall die!

824
00:35:29,733 --> 00:35:31,367
(whooshing)
For Kalin!

825
00:35:31,367 --> 00:35:33,000
- Oh, right in the love handle!

826
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:35,167
- [Tom] Jake and the Fatman
is different than I remember!

827
00:35:35,167 --> 00:35:36,733
- [Mike] (chuckling)
Jake and the Fatman.

828
00:35:36,733 --> 00:35:39,567
(crowd screaming)

829
00:35:40,733 --> 00:35:43,233
Uh, anyone know why
we're retreating?

830
00:35:43,233 --> 00:35:46,633
- Run, acursed dogs, run
back to your master Kalin!

831
00:35:46,633 --> 00:35:48,133
- Yeah, babies!

832
00:35:48,133 --> 00:35:49,733
- And tell him the same fate
awaits anyone he sends us!

833
00:35:49,733 --> 00:35:54,300
Tell him we will fight,
we will pay no tribute!

834
00:35:54,300 --> 00:35:55,733
(crowd cheering)

835
00:35:55,733 --> 00:35:57,700
- [Tom] Oh boy, we're
safe again, woo!

836
00:36:00,367 --> 00:36:01,533
(triumphant music)

837
00:36:01,533 --> 00:36:04,033
- Come wash your hands,
oh noble soldier.

838
00:36:04,033 --> 00:36:05,467
- [Mike] They're filthy!

839
00:36:05,467 --> 00:36:07,767
- He is indeed a mighty
warrior, as mighty as Durbar!

840
00:36:07,767 --> 00:36:09,300
- And of courageous of Alexi is!

841
00:36:09,300 --> 00:36:11,667
- His strength exceeds
that of Invincor!

842
00:36:11,667 --> 00:36:14,367
- For your gallantry I will
force for you a coat of armor

843
00:36:14,367 --> 00:36:16,533
finer than the Prince's
own coat of gold!

844
00:36:16,533 --> 00:36:18,000
- [Mike] Yeah, sure you will.

845
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:19,767
- Take this lance, it was
fraught for a mighty warrior!

846
00:36:19,767 --> 00:36:20,967
- [Crow] He never claimed it!

847
00:36:20,967 --> 00:36:23,400
- I thank you all, good people.

848
00:36:23,400 --> 00:36:24,633
- [Mike] I'm outta of here!

849
00:36:24,633 --> 00:36:26,433
- I shall try to be
worthy of your trust.

850
00:36:26,433 --> 00:36:27,567
- [Man] The Prince!

851
00:36:27,567 --> 00:36:29,567
- [Tom] The Royal Pants!

852
00:36:29,567 --> 00:36:30,800
- Make way for the Prince!

853
00:36:30,800 --> 00:36:32,367
- [Mike] Fabulous, the Prince!

854
00:36:35,200 --> 00:36:37,533
Ooh, it's warmer than I
thought I was out here.

855
00:36:39,667 --> 00:36:41,200
- For your service
to our people.

856
00:36:41,200 --> 00:36:42,833
- [Tom] It's dry clean only.

857
00:36:42,833 --> 00:36:44,567
- All hail Ilya Muromets!

858
00:36:44,567 --> 00:36:46,800
(crowd cheering)

859
00:36:46,800 --> 00:36:47,733
(Tom, Mike, and Crow grunting)

860
00:36:47,733 --> 00:36:49,267
- Oh, we need lighter heroes!

861
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:55,100
- Oh, once again I'm not
invited, Finland is so cliquey!

862
00:36:55,100 --> 00:36:56,800
- I must act quickly!

863
00:36:56,800 --> 00:36:59,000
I must get rid of this new hero,

864
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:00,600
else I will have to
answer for myself

865
00:37:00,600 --> 00:37:03,400
to Kalin and his terrible
band of cutthroats!

866
00:37:03,400 --> 00:37:05,033
- [Mike] Thanks for the aside.

867
00:37:05,033 --> 00:37:07,633
(upbeat music)

868
00:37:11,600 --> 00:37:13,367
- And here is your share.

869
00:37:13,367 --> 00:37:16,233
All of this, all the
gold for you, here.

870
00:37:16,233 --> 00:37:17,667
(laughing)

871
00:37:17,667 --> 00:37:19,000
And now for my share--

872
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:20,233
- [Tom] Microsoft stock!

873
00:37:20,233 --> 00:37:23,067
- I will take what is
left, the captive maid,

874
00:37:23,067 --> 00:37:25,733
who stands there waiting
anxiously for me! (laughing)

875
00:37:25,733 --> 00:37:28,933
- Let me have her, Tartak, and
you can have all my silver!

876
00:37:28,933 --> 00:37:30,200
- No, don't play
with your booby.

877
00:37:30,200 --> 00:37:31,600
- Give her to me, you
can have all the gold!

878
00:37:31,600 --> 00:37:32,833
- Not so fast!
- Ooh!

879
00:37:32,833 --> 00:37:36,400
- You shall not
have her, nor you!

880
00:37:36,400 --> 00:37:38,733
I will take the captive
maid to Chief Kalin!

881
00:37:38,733 --> 00:37:39,567
- [Mike] Ow!

882
00:37:39,567 --> 00:37:41,000
- He is sure to give me

883
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:43,733
half a kingdom for
this prize beauty!

884
00:37:43,733 --> 00:37:44,700
(grunting)

885
00:37:44,700 --> 00:37:45,933
- [Tom] Exit stage left!

886
00:37:45,933 --> 00:37:47,633
- You'll never be, you
plundering thieves!

887
00:37:47,633 --> 00:37:49,133
- Gypsies and tramps!

888
00:37:49,133 --> 00:37:52,867
- [Ilya] She will be set free
to go home to her parents!

889
00:37:52,867 --> 00:37:54,367
- [Mike] Uh, I'm
tryin' to sleep.

890
00:37:54,367 --> 00:37:57,567
- Fear not, little one, they
shall harm you no longer!

891
00:37:57,567 --> 00:37:59,133
I shall release you!

892
00:37:59,133 --> 00:38:00,600
Nothing on this Earth--

893
00:38:00,600 --> 00:38:02,067
- [Tom] Just let me
say goodbye to Glock!

894
00:38:02,067 --> 00:38:06,867
- Not even a Tugar would
keep you from me ever again.

895
00:38:08,267 --> 00:38:09,200
(crowd murmuring)

896
00:38:09,200 --> 00:38:10,033
- [Man] The Prince!

897
00:38:10,033 --> 00:38:10,967
- Look busy!

898
00:38:12,433 --> 00:38:15,100
- I see you are
quarreling again, my
rich and worthy nobles.

899
00:38:15,100 --> 00:38:16,067
- [Mike] So just
give me the remote.

900
00:38:16,067 --> 00:38:17,600
- If I gave you free rein

901
00:38:17,600 --> 00:38:20,133
you would tear our country
apart with your fighting.

902
00:38:20,133 --> 00:38:21,167
Matthew Bradoa.o

903
00:38:22,400 --> 00:38:24,300
- [Crow] You're gonna
hit me, aren't you?

904
00:38:24,300 --> 00:38:26,200
- I have work for you.

905
00:38:26,200 --> 00:38:29,067
You must prepare a caravan
of furs and copper--

906
00:38:29,067 --> 00:38:29,900
- [Mike] I'm dead.

907
00:38:29,900 --> 00:38:31,367
- And voyage out to sea!

908
00:38:31,367 --> 00:38:34,733
- [Mike] Sure I wasn't doing
anything for the next 10 years!

909
00:38:34,733 --> 00:38:35,567
(birds chirping)

910
00:38:35,567 --> 00:38:36,800
(peaceful music)

911
00:38:36,800 --> 00:38:38,067
- [Tom] It's the
Song of the South!

912
00:38:38,067 --> 00:38:41,967
(woman singing in
foreign language)

913
00:38:42,967 --> 00:38:44,567
- Woo, Freebird, come on, woo!!

914
00:38:49,600 --> 00:38:52,933
(Tom singing gibberish)

915
00:38:57,033 --> 00:38:58,100
- Ah, dinner!

916
00:39:00,533 --> 00:39:03,667
- [Tom] Johnny Mercer lyrics
really make this song.

917
00:39:03,667 --> 00:39:06,467
- [Mike] She did all the same
stuff at her last concert.

918
00:39:09,067 --> 00:39:10,733
- Okay, we all drop on three!

919
00:39:13,500 --> 00:39:15,300
It's a living!

920
00:39:15,300 --> 00:39:17,433
- [Mike] Hey, I've
got a baby to deliver!

921
00:39:18,767 --> 00:39:21,033
- [Tom] I rather be roadkill
than listen to this!

922
00:39:24,467 --> 00:39:26,267
- How 'bout a tip, lady?

923
00:39:27,700 --> 00:39:30,433
- [Mike] Well, I gotta go
spread the plague, bye!

924
00:39:33,967 --> 00:39:36,933
- [Tom] Ah, magic of Heidi,
ladies and gentlemen!

925
00:39:39,200 --> 00:39:41,633
- This song contains
satanic messages!

926
00:39:44,500 --> 00:39:45,633
- [Tom] Hey, Red Foxx!

927
00:39:47,233 --> 00:39:48,567
- Oh, Bunny Rich!

928
00:39:53,667 --> 00:39:55,933
- Still spinning and
weaving, Velia, my love?

929
00:39:55,933 --> 00:39:57,467
- [Mike] What's
with the oven mitts?

930
00:39:57,467 --> 00:40:00,500
- The lonely thoughts, it has
been lonely here without you.

931
00:40:00,500 --> 00:40:03,600
- I, too, have spent many years
of loneliness, my dear wife,

932
00:40:03,600 --> 00:40:06,733
but that is all behind me
now, I am lonely no more!

933
00:40:06,733 --> 00:40:07,967
- [Tom] I got a cat!

934
00:40:07,967 --> 00:40:09,633
- In our marriage I have
found true happiness,

935
00:40:09,633 --> 00:40:12,400
dearest Velia, a priceless gift.

936
00:40:12,400 --> 00:40:15,167
- [Mike] Now, where
the hell's my dinner?

937
00:40:15,167 --> 00:40:16,367
- But what is this?

938
00:40:16,367 --> 00:40:18,067
- [Mike] How much did this cost?

939
00:40:18,067 --> 00:40:18,900
- This cloth,

940
00:40:20,633 --> 00:40:22,167
it's woven of gold, it glitters!

941
00:40:22,167 --> 00:40:26,200
- It is not a cloth, it
is a magic tablecloth!

942
00:40:26,200 --> 00:40:28,300
- Uh-huh.
- It is beautiful indeed!

943
00:40:28,300 --> 00:40:29,600
For whom did you make it?

944
00:40:29,600 --> 00:40:30,833
- Deb's wedding shower.

945
00:40:30,833 --> 00:40:33,500
- For the one whom
I love the best!

946
00:40:33,500 --> 00:40:35,067
- The milkman?

947
00:40:35,067 --> 00:40:38,000
- Now you must rest from your
labors, my busy little wife!

948
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:40,033
- [Tom] Let us the nasty do.

949
00:40:40,033 --> 00:40:41,033
- All these wonders.

950
00:40:42,733 --> 00:40:45,867
The Earth offers it
all for us to glory in.

951
00:40:45,867 --> 00:40:49,000
- [Mike] A beautiful sunset
in Branson, Missouri!

952
00:40:54,333 --> 00:40:55,533
- [Tom] Hey, it's
the Nina, the Pinta,

953
00:40:55,533 --> 00:40:56,900
and the Mongo Santamaria!

954
00:41:02,133 --> 00:41:04,600
- (whistling) You can
almost see her hairline!

955
00:41:04,600 --> 00:41:06,867
- Grieve not, my
sweet one, grieve not.

956
00:41:08,133 --> 00:41:09,800
We do not part for long.

957
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:11,967
- [Mike] I know, that's
what I'm grieving about.

958
00:41:11,967 --> 00:41:14,600
- I shall drive Kalin
and his wicked Tugars

959
00:41:14,600 --> 00:41:17,700
from the gates of our
city once and for all

960
00:41:17,700 --> 00:41:20,867
and rid our land of those
traitors who would betray it!

961
00:41:20,867 --> 00:41:22,133
- [Tom] Okay, see
you after work!

962
00:41:22,133 --> 00:41:24,233
- In this most bitter
hour of our parting,

963
00:41:25,100 --> 00:41:26,367
tell me dearest one--

964
00:41:26,367 --> 00:41:27,600
- Can I have the checkbook?

965
00:41:27,600 --> 00:41:30,367
- Tell me truly of
your greatest wish.

966
00:41:30,367 --> 00:41:32,000
- [Mike] Pudding,
lots of pudding!

967
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:35,900
- Bear me a son,
Velia, a brave son

968
00:41:35,900 --> 00:41:38,400
to grow up strong and
be a great warrior!

969
00:41:38,400 --> 00:41:40,700
- Merlin Olsen is
no action hero.

970
00:41:40,700 --> 00:41:42,367
- The falcons in the sky,

971
00:41:43,600 --> 00:41:45,200
they were witness to
our love, little Velia.

972
00:41:45,200 --> 00:41:47,533
- [Tom, Mike, And Crow] Ew!

973
00:41:47,533 --> 00:41:51,667
- If you should bear a son,
call him Little Falcon.

974
00:41:51,667 --> 00:41:52,767
- [Tom] How 'bout Rick?

975
00:41:52,767 --> 00:41:54,767
- And whenever I see a falcon--

976
00:41:54,767 --> 00:41:56,233
- [Mike] Um, something.

977
00:41:56,233 --> 00:41:57,700
- I shall think of my son.

978
00:41:58,867 --> 00:42:00,233
- It is my greatest
wish to give you

979
00:42:00,233 --> 00:42:02,700
the son you desire, my beloved.

980
00:42:02,700 --> 00:42:04,233
- If you bear a son--

981
00:42:04,233 --> 00:42:05,433
- I want to know
who the father is.

982
00:42:05,433 --> 00:42:06,500
- Give him this ring.

983
00:42:07,667 --> 00:42:12,067
It was given to
me by our Prince.

984
00:42:12,067 --> 00:42:14,667
- [Mike] Oh, he's gonna give
her his letter jacket, too.

985
00:42:16,100 --> 00:42:18,400
- That's enough now, we're
being too demonstrative.

986
00:42:19,400 --> 00:42:20,367
(gentle music)

987
00:42:20,367 --> 00:42:23,733
♪ Headin' out to Eden yeah ♪

988
00:42:23,733 --> 00:42:25,333
- [Narrator] Once again,

989
00:42:25,333 --> 00:42:27,700
Velia was to be
separated from her love.

990
00:42:27,700 --> 00:42:29,567
- [Mike] She came over last
night and we just just talked.

991
00:42:29,567 --> 00:42:32,500
- [Narrator] Ilya, fearing
another attack by the Tugars,

992
00:42:32,500 --> 00:42:34,300
insisted that his wife accompany

993
00:42:34,300 --> 00:42:36,900
the Prince's caravan
of furs and copper.

994
00:42:37,967 --> 00:42:39,433
On the open sea
- The Gene Simmons book!

995
00:42:39,433 --> 00:42:42,600
- [Narrator] He reasoned,
Velia would be safe from harm.

996
00:42:42,600 --> 00:42:44,500
- Her singing will
keep everyone at bay!

997
00:42:44,500 --> 00:42:48,400
(Velia singing in
foreign language)

998
00:42:48,400 --> 00:42:49,567
- [Mike] Nice autoharp.

999
00:42:50,833 --> 00:42:53,133
- [Tom] Hey lady, you're
puttin' the bass down!

1000
00:42:56,900 --> 00:42:59,400
- [Mike] Wanna grab an
oar, Nana Mouskouri?

1001
00:43:07,067 --> 00:43:09,067
(crowd yelling)

1002
00:43:09,067 --> 00:43:10,300
- [Tom] Boy, he
can whip up a horde

1003
00:43:10,300 --> 00:43:12,167
faster than you can
say Jack Robinson!

1004
00:43:13,400 --> 00:43:15,100
- [Mike] No, the other way!

1005
00:43:17,733 --> 00:43:19,400
- [Tom] Hey, it's
the undersea king

1006
00:43:19,400 --> 00:43:23,033
♪ Dum dum de dum de ♪

1007
00:43:23,033 --> 00:43:24,600
- [Man] The Tugars are coming!

1008
00:43:24,600 --> 00:43:25,867
- [Tom] The British are coming?

1009
00:43:25,867 --> 00:43:27,733
- Don't leave me,
they're coming!

1010
00:43:27,733 --> 00:43:28,567
- Turn the boat!

1011
00:43:28,567 --> 00:43:29,900
(dramatic music)

1012
00:43:29,900 --> 00:43:31,600
- [Mike] The Navy
SEALs are here!

1013
00:43:38,233 --> 00:43:40,600
- Hi, I'm Julie,
your cruise director.

1014
00:43:42,733 --> 00:43:44,567
(man screaming)
- Hey you nicked me!

1015
00:43:45,567 --> 00:43:46,600
(Velia screaming)

1016
00:43:46,600 --> 00:43:48,100
- [Mike] Come to Uncle Mongol.

1017
00:43:49,667 --> 00:43:52,433
- By the gods, here
she is again, that
pretty one for Kalin!

1018
00:43:52,433 --> 00:43:53,600
- Ha ha, fine!

1019
00:43:56,367 --> 00:43:58,833
(jovial music)

1020
00:43:58,833 --> 00:44:00,767
- [Tom] Ah, the
Magnificent Torkelsons!

1021
00:44:02,567 --> 00:44:04,600
- [Mike] Greetings
from Rosemary Clooney!

1022
00:44:06,067 --> 00:44:10,467
♪ Here comes a king, here
comes a big number one ♪

1023
00:44:10,467 --> 00:44:13,600
- White Track simulated film
snow, ask for it by name.

1024
00:44:15,300 --> 00:44:18,467
♪ Do doo lee doo do lee do ♪

1025
00:44:18,467 --> 00:44:20,000
♪ We're cold, we're cold ♪

1026
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:24,567
♪ We're freezing, we're
freezing, we're freezing ♪

1027
00:44:27,033 --> 00:44:29,600
(upbeat music)

1028
00:44:33,033 --> 00:44:35,467
♪ Applesauce,
balderdash, and baloney ♪

1029
00:44:35,467 --> 00:44:38,033
♪ Flimflam foodle-diddle fudge ♪

1030
00:44:38,033 --> 00:44:40,467
♪ Hogwash, fooey,
and horsefeathers ♪

1031
00:44:40,467 --> 00:44:43,500
♪ Pithle, pish-posh,
poppycock, Pete and Pete ♪

1032
00:44:43,500 --> 00:44:46,200
♪ Ya sure you betcha! ♪

1033
00:44:46,200 --> 00:44:49,467
♪ Lutefisk Lutheran,
leather and pumpkin ♪

1034
00:44:49,467 --> 00:44:52,233
♪ Flibberty-gibbet,
phooey, yokeum ♪

1035
00:44:52,233 --> 00:44:55,033
♪ Twattle,
wangdoodle, wingding ♪

1036
00:44:55,033 --> 00:44:57,933
♪ Kickety-Knack no ♪

1037
00:45:00,833 --> 00:45:02,233
You guys so weird!

1038
00:45:04,067 --> 00:45:06,300
- But, but I'm a bunny!

1039
00:45:06,300 --> 00:45:07,400
Hop!

1040
00:45:07,400 --> 00:45:08,700
Hop!

1041
00:45:08,700 --> 00:45:10,200
Hop.
- Oh, give it up!

1042
00:45:10,200 --> 00:45:11,133
(alarm blaring)
- Hey, I'm molting!

1043
00:45:11,133 --> 00:45:12,533
- [Mike] We got movie sign!

1044
00:45:12,533 --> 00:45:14,567
- [Tom] This is the most
humilating thing I've ever done!

1045
00:45:14,567 --> 00:45:15,967
(clicking)

1046
00:45:15,967 --> 00:45:17,633
(whooshing)

1047
00:45:17,633 --> 00:45:19,967
(thudding)

1048
00:45:19,967 --> 00:45:21,167
(whirring)

1049
00:45:21,167 --> 00:45:23,400
(beeping)

1050
00:45:23,400 --> 00:45:26,667
(clanking and creaking)

1051
00:45:26,667 --> 00:45:27,933
- [Mike] Hop, hop, hop.

1052
00:45:30,467 --> 00:45:31,900
- Matthew Bradova?

1053
00:45:31,900 --> 00:45:33,733
- [Tom] You're not
wearing that, are you?

1054
00:45:33,733 --> 00:45:35,233
- What is wrong?

1055
00:45:35,233 --> 00:45:37,433
- [Mike] I'm cold and I'm
wet and I wannao go in!

1056
00:45:37,433 --> 00:45:41,633
- Punish me not, O Prince,
please let me speak first.

1057
00:45:41,633 --> 00:45:43,100
- Okay, now punish me!

1058
00:45:44,500 --> 00:45:45,367
- Speak then!

1059
00:45:46,533 --> 00:45:49,200
- We were attacked
by a band of Tugars!

1060
00:45:49,200 --> 00:45:50,633
- [Tom, Mike, And Crow] Whee!

1061
00:45:50,633 --> 00:45:53,867
- They plundered the
caravan, took everything.

1062
00:45:54,967 --> 00:45:58,200
I escaped after spending
months in bondage.

1063
00:45:58,200 --> 00:45:59,700
- That was the good part.

1064
00:46:01,167 --> 00:46:03,767
- [Tom] Damn, and the Snow Days
Festival was going so well!

1065
00:46:04,800 --> 00:46:06,700
- Ilya Muromets, ha!

1066
00:46:06,700 --> 00:46:07,633
- [Mike] That's Italian.

1067
00:46:07,633 --> 00:46:09,333
- Why was he not there to help?

1068
00:46:09,333 --> 00:46:11,400
- Did I not tell
you, Radiant Prince?

1069
00:46:11,400 --> 00:46:15,233
He is a fool, he is not the
sort of man to be trusted, sire,

1070
00:46:15,233 --> 00:46:16,700
he should've been
there to help Matthew!

1071
00:46:16,700 --> 00:46:19,800
- For this I will banish
him from the court,

1072
00:46:19,800 --> 00:46:21,233
for three full years.

1073
00:46:22,300 --> 00:46:24,400
- Throw down your hotdogs!

1074
00:46:24,400 --> 00:46:27,500
- If you banish Ilya,
you exile our strength!

1075
00:46:27,500 --> 00:46:29,100
- Fond as I am of Ilya--

1076
00:46:29,100 --> 00:46:30,000
- [Tom] I hate him!

1077
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:31,400
- This must be done!

1078
00:46:31,400 --> 00:46:34,133
He goes to the dungeon
to pay for his deed.

1079
00:46:34,133 --> 00:46:36,300
- [Mike] Executive
producer Steven Bochco.

1080
00:46:37,800 --> 00:46:39,833
- Greetings to
you, good soldiers!

1081
00:46:39,833 --> 00:46:40,767
- Hi.

1082
00:46:40,767 --> 00:46:42,300
- I see you serve our city well!

1083
00:46:42,300 --> 00:46:45,533
- There is little joy in our
service today I fear, Ilya.

1084
00:46:45,533 --> 00:46:47,000
- [Tom] I gotta work.

1085
00:46:47,000 --> 00:46:50,367
- [Soldier] Blame us not, Ilya,
the Prince has given orders,

1086
00:46:50,367 --> 00:46:51,500
you're not to enter.

1087
00:46:51,500 --> 00:46:53,833
- You jest, do you not?

1088
00:46:53,833 --> 00:46:55,633
I have ridden here
in great haste

1089
00:46:55,633 --> 00:46:58,633
to help rid the palace
of its traitors!

1090
00:46:58,633 --> 00:47:00,800
- Do not let him in the palace!

1091
00:47:00,800 --> 00:47:02,033
- [Mike] Not with his shoes on!

1092
00:47:02,033 --> 00:47:03,500
- The Prince's orders.

1093
00:47:03,500 --> 00:47:06,033
- This is your work, O
captor of the wind demon,

1094
00:47:06,033 --> 00:47:08,467
so brave and fearless
in battle, huh?

1095
00:47:09,633 --> 00:47:11,267
Velia has told me the true story

1096
00:47:11,267 --> 00:47:14,233
of your treachery and
deceit, traitorous villain!

1097
00:47:14,233 --> 00:47:15,833
- Ilya, you're not
wanted here anymore,

1098
00:47:15,833 --> 00:47:17,867
you have been banished!

1099
00:47:17,867 --> 00:47:21,067
- So you all conspire against
me, do you, my nobles?

1100
00:47:21,067 --> 00:47:22,567
- [Crow] Let me just...

1101
00:47:22,567 --> 00:47:24,700
- You will soon see how
I deal with conspirators!

1102
00:47:24,700 --> 00:47:26,100
- [Mike] Dig this!

1103
00:47:26,100 --> 00:47:27,533
(shattering)

1104
00:47:27,533 --> 00:47:28,767
- [Tom] He does gutter work!

1105
00:47:28,767 --> 00:47:30,433
- I think he should be
hanged soon as possible!

1106
00:47:30,433 --> 00:47:32,667
- I think he should be
drawn and quartered!

1107
00:47:32,667 --> 00:47:35,267
- Let the Prince
decide to do with him!

1108
00:47:35,267 --> 00:47:38,167
- If the Prince
wants no more of me,

1109
00:47:38,167 --> 00:47:40,267
then I want no more of his
gifts you may tell him!

1110
00:47:40,267 --> 00:47:41,767
(Crow whistling)

1111
00:47:41,767 --> 00:47:44,767
As I drag this coat in the
snow by its dangling sleeve--

1112
00:47:44,767 --> 00:47:45,867
- [Mike] It gets filthy!

1113
00:47:45,867 --> 00:47:47,333
- So I shall drag those traitors

1114
00:47:47,333 --> 00:47:49,033
who have plotted against me!

1115
00:47:49,033 --> 00:47:50,900
- [Tom] Here, and no starch!

1116
00:47:50,900 --> 00:47:54,500
- You nobles are ready
enough to join in a feast,

1117
00:47:54,500 --> 00:47:55,833
what about the Tugars, huh?

1118
00:47:57,000 --> 00:47:58,900
Who among you is
ready to stand up

1119
00:47:58,900 --> 00:48:00,500
and fight when the Tugars come?

1120
00:48:00,500 --> 00:48:03,700
- They are brave men they are,
when the Tugars are far away.

1121
00:48:03,700 --> 00:48:07,267
- I will drive every traitor
from the palace, I swear it!

1122
00:48:07,267 --> 00:48:09,333
- You act too hastily,
brother warrior.

1123
00:48:09,333 --> 00:48:12,000
- The Prince is quick of temper
but he cools quickly, too.

1124
00:48:12,000 --> 00:48:14,733
He has sent me to fetch you,
come to the palace with me.

1125
00:48:14,733 --> 00:48:16,733
- (growling) My
honor is at stake!

1126
00:48:16,733 --> 00:48:19,133
I'll not rest 'til I've
exposed these scoundrels!

1127
00:48:19,133 --> 00:48:20,367
(crowd shouting)

1128
00:48:20,367 --> 00:48:22,833
- He's consulting
Black Oak Arkansas.

1129
00:48:22,833 --> 00:48:26,000
- Have you forgotten the
pledge we took, Ilya Muromets?

1130
00:48:26,000 --> 00:48:28,133
The younger brother
shall heed the older?

1131
00:48:28,133 --> 00:48:30,233
That was our pledge, Ilya.

1132
00:48:30,233 --> 00:48:34,033
- Our Prince is wise and
knows whom to send here.

1133
00:48:34,033 --> 00:48:36,600
No one could persuade me
to go but you, Durbar.

1134
00:48:36,600 --> 00:48:37,867
- [Tom] Dove Bar?

1135
00:48:37,867 --> 00:48:39,533
- Come, let us go
to the palace now!

1136
00:48:39,533 --> 00:48:42,567
- [Tom] Mm! (lips smacking)

1137
00:48:42,567 --> 00:48:46,000
- [Mike] Anyway, on Melrose
Place, oh, no more, shh!

1138
00:48:46,000 --> 00:48:49,233
- Why did you draw your bow
in anger beneath my window?

1139
00:48:49,233 --> 00:48:52,600
- To avenge the wrong you did
in accusing me unjustly, sire!

1140
00:48:52,600 --> 00:48:54,133
- The arrow did
not leave his bow.

1141
00:48:54,133 --> 00:48:56,467
- He has evil thoughts
of you, O Prince.

1142
00:48:56,467 --> 00:48:59,600
I saw him trample your
coat on the ground thusly

1143
00:48:59,600 --> 00:49:01,333
and threatened to do
the same to you, sire!

1144
00:49:01,333 --> 00:49:03,367
- Yes, I heard him threatened
to that a moment ago.

1145
00:49:03,367 --> 00:49:04,300
- Yes, he did it!

1146
00:49:04,300 --> 00:49:05,467
- [Tom] You're outta order!

1147
00:49:05,467 --> 00:49:07,800
The whole damn
castle's outta order!

1148
00:49:09,067 --> 00:49:11,100
- But I did not
threaten you, My Prince.

1149
00:49:11,100 --> 00:49:12,867
- [Nobleman] He is not
to be trusted, sire.

1150
00:49:12,867 --> 00:49:15,333
- He will stir the entire
court in the mutiny, sire!

1151
00:49:15,333 --> 00:49:18,033
- There's the little matter
of an unauthorized facts!

1152
00:49:19,200 --> 00:49:22,000
- Listen, already
they are rebellious!

1153
00:49:22,000 --> 00:49:24,667
- It is not in the streets
that treachery is planned,

1154
00:49:24,667 --> 00:49:25,600
O My Prince--

1155
00:49:25,600 --> 00:49:27,133
- [Mike] It's at a Chile's!

1156
00:49:27,133 --> 00:49:29,867
- It is right here in the
palace that it is hidden!

1157
00:49:29,867 --> 00:49:32,300
- Your words are empty, Ilya.

1158
00:49:32,300 --> 00:49:33,667
They are untrue.

1159
00:49:33,667 --> 00:49:35,500
- What shall we do
with this traitor?

1160
00:49:35,500 --> 00:49:37,800
- Away with him to the dungeons.

1161
00:49:37,800 --> 00:49:39,133
Feed him bread and water.

1162
00:49:39,133 --> 00:49:41,033
- Uh, then a salad,
then an appetizer.

1163
00:49:41,033 --> 00:49:44,933
- Perhaps there he will
learn humility and wisdom.

1164
00:49:44,933 --> 00:49:46,167
- Prince Vanda, I thank you

1165
00:49:46,167 --> 00:49:48,500
for inviting me
to feast with you.

1166
00:49:48,500 --> 00:49:51,600
And you too, Durbar, for
persuading me to come.

1167
00:49:51,600 --> 00:49:53,400
- I always believed you to
be on the side of justice,

1168
00:49:53,400 --> 00:49:55,533
My Prince, let Ilya you go free.

1169
00:49:55,533 --> 00:49:57,800
- He boasted that he
would rule our country.

1170
00:49:57,800 --> 00:49:59,300
- The deed is done now.

1171
00:50:00,600 --> 00:50:01,767
Lead him away.

1172
00:50:01,767 --> 00:50:02,700
(crowd clamoring)

1173
00:50:02,700 --> 00:50:03,633
- [Tom] This is so bogus!

1174
00:50:03,633 --> 00:50:05,700
- Take him to the dungeon!

1175
00:50:05,700 --> 00:50:06,967
- [Mike] You know,
it would be easy

1176
00:50:06,967 --> 00:50:08,500
to grab the wrong
whiskery fat guy.

1177
00:50:09,967 --> 00:50:12,167
- If I so willed I could have
crumbled your palace into bits

1178
00:50:12,167 --> 00:50:14,333
but I had no wish to
spoil its decorations!

1179
00:50:15,700 --> 00:50:20,067
The hour will come, Prince
Vanda, when you will bow to me!

1180
00:50:21,567 --> 00:50:23,167
- I can be such a bitch.

1181
00:50:24,333 --> 00:50:29,067
- Now, lead me away,
lackeys and schemers,

1182
00:50:29,800 --> 00:50:31,767
I am weary of this talk.

1183
00:50:31,767 --> 00:50:34,233
- [Tom] Everybody's
talkin' at me.

1184
00:50:34,233 --> 00:50:36,567
♪ Do do do do do do do do ♪

1185
00:50:36,567 --> 00:50:38,533
- It is not Ilya
Muromets you have wronged

1186
00:50:38,533 --> 00:50:39,800
but our country herself,

1187
00:50:39,800 --> 00:50:41,500
you have taken the
sword from her hand!

1188
00:50:42,567 --> 00:50:44,433
- He speaks the truth!

1189
00:50:44,433 --> 00:50:46,800
We swear never to set
foot in the palace!

1190
00:50:46,800 --> 00:50:47,867
- [Mike] Don't we?

1191
00:50:47,867 --> 00:50:49,367
- You've banished us as well.

1192
00:50:49,367 --> 00:50:51,833
- Finland's annual
emotional outburst.

1193
00:50:54,267 --> 00:50:56,767
- [Tom] Uh, all for
one and one for all?

1194
00:50:57,967 --> 00:50:59,433
- [Mike] I'll be
in my ready room!

1195
00:51:02,467 --> 00:51:05,333
- Oh, I hate this thing, it
does not make me feel pretty!

1196
00:51:05,333 --> 00:51:09,133
- What you have done it
most unwise, my dear.

1197
00:51:09,133 --> 00:51:12,800
Let him go free, send
him away to a village.

1198
00:51:12,800 --> 00:51:15,833
He has performed many services
for our country, my dear.

1199
00:51:15,833 --> 00:51:17,100
- [Tom] My perky wife!

1200
00:51:17,100 --> 00:51:19,900
- Feed him well, mind
you, look after him.

1201
00:51:19,900 --> 00:51:21,900
- [Mike] Spread some
papers, give him a chew toy.

1202
00:51:21,900 --> 00:51:23,433
- He will repent.

1203
00:51:23,433 --> 00:51:25,967
That country bumpkin thinks
himself higher than the Prince,

1204
00:51:25,967 --> 00:51:28,867
he is much too proud,
he will never repent!

1205
00:51:28,867 --> 00:51:30,800
- Feed him well, I tell you.

1206
00:51:30,800 --> 00:51:32,800
Feed him well, I commanded it!

1207
00:51:32,800 --> 00:51:34,933
- [Tom] So they fed
him ice and water.

1208
00:51:36,300 --> 00:51:39,100
- Oh, the ice seems safe,
let's drive our pickup onto it.

1209
00:51:41,700 --> 00:51:45,067
- [Mike] Yes, Finland is a
four season vacation paradise.

1210
00:51:47,633 --> 00:51:50,267
- [Tom] I always get put
right next to the ice machine.

1211
00:51:50,267 --> 00:51:51,767
- [Mike] July in Minnesota!

1212
00:51:51,767 --> 00:51:54,333
(all chuckling)

1213
00:51:54,333 --> 00:51:57,100
- Okay, we get it, the
cycle of friggin' life!

1214
00:51:58,900 --> 00:52:00,633
- [Tom] I think
it's a film on sex.

1215
00:52:03,000 --> 00:52:04,733
- Feed him well, he tells me.

1216
00:52:04,733 --> 00:52:06,733
- [Mike] This legend could've
used some punching up.

1217
00:52:06,733 --> 00:52:09,200
- [Tom] The Legend of
Boggy Creek had more depth!

1218
00:52:13,200 --> 00:52:15,600
- That I have not
done nor will I!

1219
00:52:15,600 --> 00:52:17,467
- [Mike] Just empty
the chamberpot!

1220
00:52:17,467 --> 00:52:19,667
- He must've died of hunger.

1221
00:52:19,667 --> 00:52:21,200
Seven moons have passed.

1222
00:52:22,500 --> 00:52:24,733
I must send a signal to Sartack.

1223
00:52:24,733 --> 00:52:26,100
Now, swift river, you must help.

1224
00:52:26,100 --> 00:52:28,067
Carry my message to the Tugars

1225
00:52:28,067 --> 00:52:29,633
who wait this promised signal,

1226
00:52:29,633 --> 00:52:31,567
which will be the
sign to attack!

1227
00:52:34,100 --> 00:52:36,233
(splashing)
- I love you, fish!

1228
00:52:36,233 --> 00:52:37,267
- Hey!

1229
00:52:37,267 --> 00:52:40,000
What're you doing up there, eh?

1230
00:52:40,000 --> 00:52:42,867
- Uh, oh, heaven help me,
there was someone down!

1231
00:52:42,867 --> 00:52:46,033
- Whoa, whoa, I'm
Robin Williams, oh, oh!

1232
00:52:46,033 --> 00:52:47,800
(tearing)
- Oh, I could go

1233
00:52:47,800 --> 00:52:49,867
my whole life
without seein' that.

1234
00:52:51,733 --> 00:52:56,000
♪ And they call him the Streak ♪

1235
00:52:56,000 --> 00:52:57,667
- I smell fresh pants!

1236
00:52:59,533 --> 00:53:01,533
- [Tom] I'll make myself a
soup out of these trousers!

1237
00:53:01,533 --> 00:53:04,000
- Ah, this is strange.

1238
00:53:05,400 --> 00:53:09,933
I set a trap for a fox, I catch
a pair of breeches instead!

1239
00:53:09,933 --> 00:53:11,367
- [Mike] Now I am folding them

1240
00:53:11,367 --> 00:53:13,433
and now I'm holding this up!

1241
00:53:13,433 --> 00:53:16,467
- This key looks familiar,
I have seen it before.

1242
00:53:18,400 --> 00:53:19,600
- [Mike] Bending over now.

1243
00:53:20,633 --> 00:53:23,400
- Ah, this looks like trickery!

1244
00:53:24,633 --> 00:53:25,833
That devil is a sly one!

1245
00:53:26,700 --> 00:53:28,033
But I can play trick too.

1246
00:53:28,033 --> 00:53:30,233
- [Mike] Hey, you don't
need to convince us!

1247
00:53:30,233 --> 00:53:33,067
- Wacky prop comic,
Lutefisk Top!

1248
00:53:33,067 --> 00:53:34,067
- Wherever you like!

1249
00:53:34,967 --> 00:53:36,867
Where the tide takes you!

1250
00:53:36,867 --> 00:53:38,333
Beyond the Seventh Sea!

1251
00:53:38,333 --> 00:53:41,100
- [Tom] Yeah this scene sure
brings a film into sharp focus.

1252
00:53:42,667 --> 00:53:43,767
(dramatic music)

1253
00:53:43,767 --> 00:53:46,700
- Joyous news, O Exalted One!

1254
00:53:46,700 --> 00:53:48,167
- [Mike] I'm a bird, go away.

1255
00:53:48,167 --> 00:53:49,967
- Some passing merchants
have told me of the Prince.

1256
00:53:49,967 --> 00:53:51,133
- [Tom] Got my headphones on!

1257
00:53:51,133 --> 00:53:53,233
- He has thrown
Muromet into a prison

1258
00:53:53,233 --> 00:53:56,333
but all the nobles are
deserting for a home

1259
00:53:56,333 --> 00:53:59,300
and refusing to
fight! (laughing)

1260
00:53:59,300 --> 00:54:01,167
(Tom, Mike, and Crow laughing)

1261
00:54:01,167 --> 00:54:02,067
- Bring good news.

1262
00:54:03,167 --> 00:54:06,400
I'll destroy the infidel
who dare defy me!

1263
00:54:06,400 --> 00:54:08,033
- It's Boris Badenov!

1264
00:54:08,033 --> 00:54:09,400
- Saddle the horses!

1265
00:54:09,400 --> 00:54:10,633
(ominous music)

1266
00:54:10,633 --> 00:54:12,767
- [Mike] Oh, Siegfried & Roy!

1267
00:54:12,767 --> 00:54:15,033
- [Tom] Get that horse
out of my living room!

1268
00:54:16,767 --> 00:54:20,100
- The signal, we have just
found it in the river!

1269
00:54:20,100 --> 00:54:22,167
He kept his word, that sly one!

1270
00:54:22,167 --> 00:54:23,933
This was the single
pre-arranged.

1271
00:54:23,933 --> 00:54:26,167
Once again, Kalin,
I served you well!

1272
00:54:26,167 --> 00:54:27,367
- Let me see what you have.

1273
00:54:27,367 --> 00:54:28,200
- [Tom] Drop 'em!

1274
00:54:30,667 --> 00:54:32,600
- [Crow] He sent a pantagram!

1275
00:54:32,600 --> 00:54:34,400
- [Tom] I ordered Heather!

1276
00:54:34,400 --> 00:54:36,900
- By Beelzebub, a
pair of breeches!

1277
00:54:38,467 --> 00:54:41,000
- These pants have stirred
something deep inside me!

1278
00:54:41,000 --> 00:54:43,100
- What does it signify to you?

1279
00:54:43,100 --> 00:54:45,600
- [Mike] It signifies
the man had a large can.

1280
00:54:47,400 --> 00:54:49,400
- They are ready to
surrender to Kalin.

1281
00:54:50,933 --> 00:54:52,500
- [Tom] Blossom was
really funny last night

1282
00:54:52,500 --> 00:54:55,400
- You see, these
breeches are a symbol

1283
00:54:55,400 --> 00:54:57,267
of the unconquerable
might of Kalin!

1284
00:54:57,267 --> 00:54:58,500
- And we'll take them in!

1285
00:54:58,500 --> 00:55:01,300
- As it were, each
ready to herald

1286
00:55:01,300 --> 00:55:03,767
the power and glory
that is Kalin.

1287
00:55:03,767 --> 00:55:06,100
- [Mike] I don't know what
I'm talking about here.

1288
00:55:06,100 --> 00:55:08,367
- I see two roads here

1289
00:55:08,367 --> 00:55:10,933
and both of them will
lead Kalin to victory.

1290
00:55:12,067 --> 00:55:15,167
- Yes, victory shall
be ours finally.

1291
00:55:15,167 --> 00:55:17,167
- [Tom] Ah, the Golden
Age of makin' stuff up!

1292
00:55:17,167 --> 00:55:19,667
- The attack must be timed
according to the stars.

1293
00:55:20,900 --> 00:55:22,033
- You are correct.

1294
00:55:22,033 --> 00:55:22,867
- Sir!

1295
00:55:24,000 --> 00:55:25,367
- It is not yet time to attack

1296
00:55:25,367 --> 00:55:27,567
until the gods of
battle tell us.

1297
00:55:27,567 --> 00:55:29,300
We will bide our time.

1298
00:55:29,300 --> 00:55:31,167
- [Tom] We will wear our pants!

1299
00:55:31,167 --> 00:55:33,167
- Unsaddle all the horses!

1300
00:55:33,167 --> 00:55:34,367
- [Mike] Okay!

1301
00:55:35,833 --> 00:55:39,000
- [Narrator] and while Kalin
waited for a favorable sign,

1302
00:55:39,000 --> 00:55:42,833
Ilya Muromets rotted
in a dark dungeon,

1303
00:55:42,833 --> 00:55:44,733
unaware that his wife had borne

1304
00:55:44,733 --> 00:55:47,567
the son he so fervently wanted.

1305
00:55:48,500 --> 00:55:51,067
And so the months slipped by.

1306
00:55:51,067 --> 00:55:52,300
- [Tom] Like a pair of pants.

1307
00:55:52,300 --> 00:55:54,600
- You are still only a baby

1308
00:55:54,600 --> 00:55:56,467
and already stronger
than an oak.

1309
00:55:56,467 --> 00:55:57,667
- And dumber than a hammer!

1310
00:55:57,667 --> 00:56:00,067
- Grow, my son,
grow tall and strong

1311
00:56:00,067 --> 00:56:01,767
and be like your father!

1312
00:56:01,767 --> 00:56:03,367
- [Mike] I'm tryin'! (grunting)

1313
00:56:03,367 --> 00:56:04,600
- With courage like his.

1314
00:56:04,600 --> 00:56:06,200
- [Tom] I don't wannao
watch Power Rangers!

1315
00:56:06,200 --> 00:56:07,567
- And his strength as well.

1316
00:56:07,567 --> 00:56:09,333
- [Mike] Can I get
some breakfast or what?

1317
00:56:09,333 --> 00:56:14,000
- Little Falcon, my son, this
is your present from him.

1318
00:56:14,000 --> 00:56:15,800
- Is my face as
weird as it feels?

1319
00:56:15,800 --> 00:56:18,800
(creaking)

1320
00:56:18,800 --> 00:56:20,100
- [Tom] Burgers are ready!

1321
00:56:26,400 --> 00:56:27,233
- [Mike] Well...

1322
00:56:28,067 --> 00:56:30,000
Kiss your aunt Bernice!

1323
00:56:31,167 --> 00:56:33,867
- Run along and
play, little one.

1324
00:56:33,867 --> 00:56:35,100
- [Tom] Oh, thanks, what's the
draw strength on this thing?

1325
00:56:35,100 --> 00:56:36,600
Could I take down an elk?

1326
00:56:38,600 --> 00:56:39,767
- Why do you not love me?

1327
00:56:39,767 --> 00:56:40,600
- [Mike] You look like RuPaul!

1328
00:56:40,600 --> 00:56:43,367
- Why do you run away?

1329
00:56:43,367 --> 00:56:45,133
How many times must I tell you

1330
00:56:45,133 --> 00:56:46,833
I wish to keep you for my own?

1331
00:56:46,833 --> 00:56:48,433
- Never, I despise you!

1332
00:56:48,433 --> 00:56:50,867
- He has an outtie in
the middle of his head!

1333
00:56:50,867 --> 00:56:52,367
- [Tom] Who loves ya, baby?

1334
00:56:52,367 --> 00:56:54,833
- You shall never touch me,
Kalin, I swear it on my life!

1335
00:56:54,833 --> 00:56:57,500
What manner of man
are you to force me?

1336
00:56:57,500 --> 00:57:00,300
- Kings grovel at my feet
and so will you, my dear.

1337
00:57:01,733 --> 00:57:04,100
- I would sooner you threw me
into a cage of wild animals!

1338
00:57:04,100 --> 00:57:05,033
- [Mike] Mm, done and done.

1339
00:57:05,033 --> 00:57:06,667
- You will never have me!

1340
00:57:06,667 --> 00:57:08,867
(Kalin laughing)
- I do need a father, Mom.

1341
00:57:08,867 --> 00:57:09,700
(Velia gasping)

1342
00:57:09,700 --> 00:57:10,533
(thudding)

1343
00:57:10,533 --> 00:57:11,467
- I will kill you!

1344
00:57:11,467 --> 00:57:13,333
- [Tom] For God and country!

1345
00:57:13,333 --> 00:57:15,667
- Ah, the little wolf cub.

1346
00:57:15,667 --> 00:57:19,333
He fights, eh? (laughing)

1347
00:57:19,333 --> 00:57:20,567
- [Mike] I got it handled, Mom.

1348
00:57:20,567 --> 00:57:22,633
(Kalin grunting)
(Velia shrieking)

1349
00:57:22,633 --> 00:57:24,133
- [Tom] What, I'm a Mongol!

1350
00:57:24,133 --> 00:57:26,700
- I shall teach you how to fight

1351
00:57:26,700 --> 00:57:30,433
and your enemy shall
be the cursed Prince!

1352
00:57:30,433 --> 00:57:31,367
- Sound all right.

1353
00:57:33,000 --> 00:57:34,267
(tense music)

1354
00:57:34,267 --> 00:57:36,800
- [Mike] Uncle B.O., can
I shoot you in the back?

1355
00:57:38,667 --> 00:57:40,967
(thudding)
- Oh, jeez!

1356
00:57:40,967 --> 00:57:43,333
- [Mike] Frampton Comes Alive!

1357
00:57:43,333 --> 00:57:45,367
(thudding)
- Ow, jeez!

1358
00:57:45,367 --> 00:57:48,067
- [Mike] I've never had a
damn thing, it's astounding!

1359
00:57:48,067 --> 00:57:50,167
- You are still a
boy, Little Falcon,

1360
00:57:50,167 --> 00:57:52,400
and already you have the
strength of a warrior!

1361
00:57:52,400 --> 00:57:55,467
You shall challenge our
champion to a jousting bout.

1362
00:57:55,467 --> 00:57:57,667
- [Tom] We'll put
it on pay-per-view!

1363
00:57:57,667 --> 00:58:01,100
- [Kalin] Show us, Little
Falcon, whom I call my son,

1364
00:58:01,100 --> 00:58:03,633
how skillfully
you wield a lance.

1365
00:58:03,633 --> 00:58:04,833
- Michael Keaton!

1366
00:58:04,833 --> 00:58:06,500
- [Kalin] I know I
shall be proud of you.

1367
00:58:06,500 --> 00:58:08,300
(trumpets sounding)

1368
00:58:08,300 --> 00:58:10,367
- [Tom] The Tower of
Gourd's horn section!

1369
00:58:13,000 --> 00:58:14,567
- [Mike] What do I do with this?

1370
00:58:14,567 --> 00:58:16,400
(dramatic music)

1371
00:58:16,400 --> 00:58:18,033
(crowd shouting)

1372
00:58:18,033 --> 00:58:19,000
(yelling)

1373
00:58:19,000 --> 00:58:20,433
- (laughing) That's funny!

1374
00:58:22,033 --> 00:58:22,867
- [Mike] Where's he goin'?

1375
00:58:22,867 --> 00:58:23,700
Jerry!

1376
00:58:28,733 --> 00:58:29,567
- That's it?

1377
00:58:29,567 --> 00:58:31,000
I want my money back!

1378
00:58:32,467 --> 00:58:35,000
- [Tom] Shouldn't there be
a dragon around pretty soon?

1379
00:58:38,767 --> 00:58:39,967
(Kalin laughing)

1380
00:58:39,967 --> 00:58:40,833
- [Mike] What're
you laughin', what?

1381
00:58:40,833 --> 00:58:42,033
I don't get it, what?

1382
00:58:42,033 --> 00:58:44,167
- To the dungeon
with this weakling!

1383
00:58:44,167 --> 00:58:46,500
Let him guard the captives!

1384
00:58:46,500 --> 00:58:48,500
(laughing)

1385
00:58:48,500 --> 00:58:50,167
- [Crow] Sorry, something I ate.

1386
00:58:50,167 --> 00:58:53,433
(horse whinnying)

1387
00:58:53,433 --> 00:58:55,133
- Well done, Little Falcon!

1388
00:58:55,133 --> 00:58:58,400
You have earned the cap of
champion to wear as your own.

1389
00:58:58,400 --> 00:59:01,433
- [Tom] Now Mongolian
stir-fry for everyone!

1390
00:59:02,667 --> 00:59:05,133
- The time has come
to take up our arms!

1391
00:59:06,200 --> 00:59:07,633
We move at last.

1392
00:59:08,700 --> 00:59:10,167
(dramatic music)

1393
00:59:10,167 --> 00:59:12,267
- Wow, now that is a horde!

1394
00:59:12,267 --> 00:59:14,600
- [Mike] This is a
free festival now, man!

1395
00:59:14,600 --> 00:59:17,267
- I wish we had the yogurt
franchise for this horde.

1396
00:59:18,467 --> 00:59:20,400
- [Tom] It's kind of
a Mingus jazzy feel.

1397
00:59:21,633 --> 00:59:24,233
(Tom warbling)

1398
00:59:26,067 --> 00:59:27,833
- [Mike] Hello
little Mongol horde!

1399
00:59:31,567 --> 00:59:34,000
- [Tom] A giant pair
of pants back there!

1400
00:59:34,000 --> 00:59:36,700
- So they walked from
China to Finland?

1401
00:59:38,567 --> 00:59:39,800
- [Mike] Are we
goin' the right way?

1402
00:59:39,800 --> 00:59:41,733
- I'm just followin'
you, I don't know!

1403
00:59:45,200 --> 00:59:47,900
- [Tom] One guy following
along with a pooper-scooper.

1404
00:59:47,900 --> 00:59:50,767
- [Mike] Sounds like a concerto
for timpani and car horn.

1405
00:59:53,033 --> 00:59:54,400
- I'm going to
Helsinki to personally

1406
00:59:54,400 --> 00:59:56,600
spear that stump-throwing
son of a bitch!

1407
00:59:56,600 --> 00:59:58,167
- [Tom] Will the
Lawrence of Arabia people

1408
00:59:58,167 --> 00:59:59,767
please get to their proper sets?

1409
01:00:04,267 --> 01:00:07,667
(Mike humming)

1410
01:00:07,667 --> 01:00:10,600
- [Mike] No, keep it open,
oh great, our plan is ruined!

1411
01:00:10,600 --> 01:00:15,467
- [Raider] Give us 700 carts
filled with gold, Prince Vanda,

1412
01:00:15,467 --> 01:00:18,600
or prepares to surrender
yourself as hostage!

1413
01:00:18,600 --> 01:00:23,467
Almighty Chief Kalin gives
you three hours to reply.

1414
01:00:23,467 --> 01:00:26,633
If you refuse, your bones
will bleach you the sun!

1415
01:00:26,633 --> 01:00:28,300
- [Tom] It's a White
Sox pennant, I think.

1416
01:00:28,300 --> 01:00:30,367
- [Raider] We will take
your princess captive

1417
01:00:30,367 --> 01:00:32,100
for the pleasure of our chief!

1418
01:00:32,100 --> 01:00:34,133
- Give this reply to Kalin--

1419
01:00:34,133 --> 01:00:35,067
(Crow imitating fart)

1420
01:00:35,067 --> 01:00:36,600
What you have demanded we will

1421
01:00:36,600 --> 01:00:39,400
pay you in three days from now.

1422
01:00:39,400 --> 01:00:41,633
- [Mike] We have to call
and clear it with the bank.

1423
01:00:41,633 --> 01:00:42,600
- [Raider] You must
bring your tribute

1424
01:00:42,600 --> 01:00:44,833
to Kalin's camp at the river!

1425
01:00:46,333 --> 01:00:49,867
- Well, which of your nobles
will you send to fight them?

1426
01:00:50,767 --> 01:00:52,367
Here they are, choose one!

1427
01:00:52,367 --> 01:00:53,900
- Uh, heh, I gotta back
- I got a chiropractor

1428
01:00:53,900 --> 01:00:55,700
- To that thing I was going.
- Gee, look at the time, wow!

1429
01:00:55,700 --> 01:00:58,400
- He spoke truly, Ilya Muromets,

1430
01:00:58,400 --> 01:01:01,367
when he said there would
be many to feast with you

1431
01:01:01,367 --> 01:01:03,833
but none to stand
up for our land.

1432
01:01:03,833 --> 01:01:05,000
He spoke wisely!

1433
01:01:05,000 --> 01:01:06,700
- [Tom] Hey, you Mongols
need another wife?

1434
01:01:06,700 --> 01:01:09,233
- Oh, if only Ilya were with us,

1435
01:01:09,233 --> 01:01:11,133
this Kalin would not
keep us in terror!

1436
01:01:11,133 --> 01:01:13,167
- A collie is keeping
them in terror?

1437
01:01:13,167 --> 01:01:16,167
- I shall go to him and
ask his forgiveness.

1438
01:01:16,167 --> 01:01:18,967
- Prince, Radiant
Prince, he may be dead!

1439
01:01:18,967 --> 01:01:20,933
He has refused food
and drink (yelping).

1440
01:01:20,933 --> 01:01:22,567
- Why have you
kept this from me?

1441
01:01:22,567 --> 01:01:24,133
Open the dungeon!

1442
01:01:24,133 --> 01:01:25,667
You'll pay for this!

1443
01:01:25,667 --> 01:01:27,667
- [Mike] You hold a Finn by
the beard it mobilizes him.

1444
01:01:27,667 --> 01:01:30,367
- Wait here, Radiant Prince,
I must run and fetch the key,

1445
01:01:30,367 --> 01:01:32,167
I do not have it with me.

1446
01:01:32,167 --> 01:01:33,633
- Is this not the key?

1447
01:01:33,633 --> 01:01:36,000
I believe this is the
key to the dungeon, sire!

1448
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:38,933
- [Tom] We have a damn
confusing kingdom here!

1449
01:01:38,933 --> 01:01:41,500
(upbeat music)

1450
01:01:45,200 --> 01:01:47,133
(tense music)

1451
01:01:47,133 --> 01:01:49,167
- So, you wily scoundrel,

1452
01:01:49,167 --> 01:01:51,600
you starved him to
death, son of misery!

1453
01:01:51,600 --> 01:01:55,300
- [Tom] (snoring) Hey, I just
got to sleep after 20 years!

1454
01:01:55,300 --> 01:01:56,933
- [Princess] He is alive, alive!

1455
01:01:56,933 --> 01:01:58,467
- Well, as alive as
a Finn gets, anyway.

1456
01:01:58,467 --> 01:02:00,700
- He lives, he is alive!

1457
01:02:01,867 --> 01:02:04,567
- I fed him, Prince,
as you commanded!

1458
01:02:04,567 --> 01:02:05,967
- He lies, my Prince.

1459
01:02:07,133 --> 01:02:09,233
He is the traitor who
has plotted against you.

1460
01:02:09,233 --> 01:02:10,667
- [Mike] He's got bedhead.

1461
01:02:10,667 --> 01:02:12,367
